ng_bibles":{"en":"eng-kjv","ar":"arb-vd","el":"grcorth","ru":"russyn","zh":"cmn-cu89s","fr":"fraLSG","hi":"hin2017","es":"spaRV1909","tl":"tglulb"}}</script></div></section><section id="adventure-trail" class="kjt-trail" aria-labelledby="kjt-trail-heading"><div class="kjt-trail__wrap"><div class="kk-banner kk-banner--dark" style="--kb1:#F3C548;--kb2:#FF9F4A"><span class="kk-banner__badge" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-core/assets/kids-extras/cards/trail.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><div class="kk-banner__text"><p class="kjt-trail__eyebrow">Kids Corner · Adventure</p><h2 id="kjt-trail-heading" class="kjt-trail__title">Bible Adventure Trail</h2><p class="kjt-trail__tagline">Learn it. Live it. Share it.</p><p class="kjt-trail__intro">Come on a journey with Jesus! Pick a stop, hear the story, answer the questions, play a game, and collect your stars.</p></div></div><div class="kjt-trail__app" data-kjt-trail><h3 class="kjt-trail__trail-name">🌿 Old Testament Trail</h3><ol class="kjt-trail__fallback"><li><strong>🌿 God Makes the World</strong> — In the very beginning there was nothing at all, only God. Then God spoke, and light shone! God made the sky, the sea, the land, the animals, and people too.</li><li><strong>⛵ Noah’s Ark</strong> — Long ago, many people had forgotten God. But Noah loved God and listened to Him. God asked Noah to build a very big boat called an ark.</li><li><strong>👑 David and Goliath</strong> — David was a young shepherd who looked after his father&#039;s sheep. When everyone else was afraid of a giant called Goliath, David remembered that God was with him.</li><li><strong>✨ God’s Promise to Abraham</strong> — God asked Abraham to leave his home and go to a new land. Abraham did not know the way, but he trusted God, and God made him a wonderful promise.</li><li><strong>🧥 Joseph and His Colourful Coat</strong> — Joseph was his father&#039;s favourite son, and he had a beautiful coat of many colours. His brothers were jealous, but God had a plan for Joseph.</li><li><strong>🌊 Moses and the Red Sea</strong> — God&#039;s people were slaves in Egypt. God chose Moses to lead them to freedom, and then He did something amazing at the sea.</li><li><strong>🐋 Jonah and the Great Fish</strong> — God asked Jonah to go to the city of Nineveh, but Jonah ran the other way. God did not give up on Jonah, or on Nineveh.</li><li><strong>🦁 Daniel in the Lions’ Den</strong> — Daniel loved God and prayed to Him every day. When a law said he must stop praying, Daniel kept praying anyway.</li></ol><h3 class="kjt-trail__trail-name">☦ Jesus Trail</h3><ol class="kjt-trail__fallback"><li><strong>⭐ The Birth of Jesus</strong> — God made a wonderful promise: He would send a Saviour. One night, in the little town of Bethlehem, that promise came true. Jesus was born!</li><li><strong>☦ Christ Is Risen!</strong> — Jesus died on the cross for us, and His friends were very sad. But on the third day, something amazing happened. Christ is risen!</li><li><strong>🕊 The Baptism of Jesus</strong> — When Jesus was grown up, He came to the River Jordan to be baptised by John. Something wonderful happened that showed us who God is.</li><li><strong>⛵ Jesus Calms the Storm</strong> — Jesus and His friends were crossing the lake in a boat when a huge storm came. The friends were terrified, but Jesus was fast asleep.</li><li><strong>🍞 Jesus Feeds Five Thousand</strong> — A huge crowd followed Jesus to listen to Him. When everyone grew hungry, a boy shared his small lunch, and Jesus did something amazing.</li><li><strong>🐑 The Lost Sheep</strong> — Jesus told a story about a shepherd who had a hundred sheep. When one sheep got lost, the shepherd went looking for it.</li><li><strong>🌳 Zacchaeus Meets Jesus</strong> — Zacchaeus was a rich tax collector, and he was very short. He wanted to see Jesus so much that he climbed a tree!</li></ol><h3 class="kjt-trail__trail-name">🕯 Saints Trail</h3><ol class="kjt-trail__fallback"><li><strong>🎁 Saint Nicholas</strong> — Long ago there lived a kind bishop called Nicholas. He loved Jesus so much that he loved to help people in need, and he did it quietly, without wanting any praise.</li><li><strong>🛡 Saint George</strong> — George was a brave soldier who loved Jesus. When he was told to stop following Jesus, George chose to stay faithful, no matter what.</li><li><strong>🐑 Saint Spyridon</strong> — Spyridon was a humble shepherd on the island of Cyprus. He loved God so much that he became a bishop, but he never stopped caring for his sheep, or for people.</li></ol></div><script type="application/json" id="kjt-trail-data">{"trails":[{"key":"old-testament","name":"🌿 Old Testament Trail","stops":[{"slug":"creation","title":"God Makes the World","icon":"🌿","image":"","discover":"In the very beginning there was nothing at all, only God. Then God spoke, and light shone! God made the sky, the sea, the land, the animals, and people too.","story":"\u003Cp\u003EBefore anything else existed, God was there. God spoke, and there was light. He called the light day and the darkness night.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EGod made the sky high above and gathered the seas so dry land could appear. He filled the land with grass, flowers and fruit trees.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EGod put the sun, the moon and the stars in the sky. He filled the seas with fish and the air with birds. He made animals of every kind.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThen God made people, a man and a woman, to know Him, love Him and care for His world. God looked at everything He had made, and it was very good.\u003C/p\u003E\n","refLabel":"Genesis 1","bibleUrl":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/read/eng-kjv/Genesis/1/1","audio":"","quiz":[{"q":"Who made the world?","a":"The animals","b":"God","c":"The sun","correct":"b"},{"q":"What did God make first?","a":"Light","b":"Fish","c":"Mountains","correct":"a"},{"q":"What did God say about everything He made?","a":"It was too big","b":"It was very good","c":"It was finished too fast","correct":"b"}],"steps":["God made light","God made the sky, the sea and the land","God made the fish and the birds","God made the animals and people"],"verse":"In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth.","verseRef":"Genesis 1:1","missing":"God","prayer":"Thank You, God, for making the whole world: the sky, the trees, the animals, and me. Help me to take care of everything You made. Amen.","lesson":"God made everything, and He made me too."},{"slug":"noahs-ark","title":"Noah’s Ark","icon":"⛵","image":"","discover":"Long ago, many people had forgotten God. But Noah loved God and listened to Him. God asked Noah to build a very big boat called an ark.","story":"\u003Cp\u003EGod told Noah that a great flood was coming. He asked Noah to build a huge wooden boat, an ark, to keep his family safe.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003ENoah trusted God and did everything God asked. When the ark was ready, the animals came, two by two, and Noah's family went inside.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThen the rain began. It rained for forty days and forty nights, and water covered the land. But the ark floated safely on the water.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EAt last the rain stopped. Noah sent out a dove, and it came back with an olive leaf. The land was drying! When everyone came out of the ark, God put a rainbow in the sky. God called it His bow, a sign of His promise never to flood the whole earth again.\u003C/p\u003E\n","refLabel":"Genesis 6–9","bibleUrl":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/read/eng-kjv/Genesis/6/9","audio":"","quiz":[{"q":"Who asked Noah to build the ark?","a":"God","b":"His neighbours","c":"The animals","correct":"a"},{"q":"What did the dove bring back?","a":"A shell","b":"An olive leaf","c":"A fish","correct":"b"},{"q":"What did God put in the sky as a promise?","a":"A star","b":"A rainbow","c":"A cloud shaped like a boat","correct":"b"}],"steps":["Noah built the ark","The animals came into the ark","It rained for forty days and forty nights","God put a rainbow in the sky"],"verse":"I do set my bow in the cloud, and it shall be for a token of a covenant between me and the earth.","verseRef":"Genesis 9:13","missing":"bow","prayer":"Dear God, thank You for keeping Noah and his family safe. Help me to listen to You and trust Your promises, just like Noah did. Amen.","lesson":"God always keeps His promises."},{"slug":"david-and-goliath","title":"David and Goliath","icon":"👑","image":"","discover":"David was a young shepherd who looked after his father's sheep. When everyone else was afraid of a giant called Goliath, David remembered that God was with him.","story":"\u003Cp\u003EEvery day, a giant soldier called Goliath shouted at God's people. He was very tall and very strong, and all the soldiers were afraid of him.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EDavid came to bring food to his brothers. When he heard Goliath, he said, \"I will go! God has helped me before, and He will help me now.\"\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EKing Saul gave David his armour, but it was far too big. So David took his shepherd's staff and his sling, and chose five smooth stones from a stream.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EDavid told Goliath, \"I come to you in the name of the Lord.\" He swung his sling, and the stone hit Goliath on the forehead. The giant fell down! Everyone saw that the battle belonged to God.\u003C/p\u003E\n","refLabel":"1 Samuel 17","bibleUrl":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/read/eng-kjv/1%20Samuel/17/1","audio":"","quiz":[{"q":"Who did David trust?","a":"His sword","b":"God","c":"His armour","correct":"b"},{"q":"What was David's job?","a":"Shepherd","b":"Baker","c":"Fisherman","correct":"a"},{"q":"How many smooth stones did David choose?","a":"Two","b":"Five","c":"Ten","correct":"b"}],"steps":["David looked after his sheep","David heard Goliath shouting","David chose five smooth stones","David trusted God and Goliath fell"],"verse":"What time I am afraid, I will trust in thee.","verseRef":"Psalm 56:3","missing":"trust","prayer":"Dear God, when I feel afraid, help me remember that You are with me. Make me brave like David. Amen.","lesson":"God helps me when I am afraid."},{"slug":"abrahams-promise","title":"God’s Promise to Abraham","icon":"✨","image":"","discover":"God asked Abraham to leave his home and go to a new land. Abraham did not know the way, but he trusted God, and God made him a wonderful promise.","story":"\u003Cp\u003EAbraham lived in a land called Ur. One day God said, “Leave your country and go to the land I will show you.”\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EAbraham packed up his tents, his animals and his family, and set off. He did not know where he was going, but he knew God would lead him.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EOne night God took Abraham outside and said, “Look up at the sky and count the stars, if you can. Your family will be as many as the stars!”\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EAbraham and Sarah were very old and had no children, but Abraham believed God. Years later, God kept His promise, and baby Isaac was born.\u003C/p\u003E\n","refLabel":"Genesis 12 and 15","bibleUrl":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/read/eng-kjv/Genesis/12/1","audio":"","quiz":[{"q":"Who asked Abraham to leave his home?","a":"His neighbours","b":"God","c":"A king","correct":"b"},{"q":"What did God tell Abraham to count?","a":"The stars","b":"The sheep","c":"The trees","correct":"a"},{"q":"What was the name of Abraham's son?","a":"Joseph","b":"Isaac","c":"Samuel","correct":"b"}],"steps":["God told Abraham to leave his home","Abraham travelled with his family and animals","God showed Abraham the stars","Baby Isaac was born"],"verse":"Look now toward heaven, and tell the stars, if thou be able to number them.","verseRef":"Genesis 15:5","missing":"stars","prayer":"Dear God, thank You that You always keep Your promises. Help me to trust You like Abraham, even when I cannot see the way. Amen.","lesson":"I can trust God to lead me."},{"slug":"josephs-coat","title":"Joseph and His Colourful Coat","icon":"🧥","image":"","discover":"Joseph was his father's favourite son, and he had a beautiful coat of many colours. His brothers were jealous, but God had a plan for Joseph.","story":"\u003Cp\u003EJacob gave his son Joseph a coat of many colours. Joseph's brothers were jealous and angry.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThey sold Joseph to travellers, who took him far away to Egypt. Joseph was sad and lonely, but God was with him.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EIn Egypt, God helped Joseph to understand Pharaoh's dreams: seven good years of food would be followed by seven hungry years. Pharaoh put Joseph in charge of storing food.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWhen the hungry years came, Joseph's brothers came to Egypt to buy food. Joseph forgave them and hugged them. God had turned something bad into something good.\u003C/p\u003E\n","refLabel":"Genesis 37 to 45","bibleUrl":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/read/eng-kjv/Genesis/37/1","audio":"","quiz":[{"q":"What did Jacob give to Joseph?","a":"A colourful coat","b":"A golden crown","c":"A shepherd's staff","correct":"a"},{"q":"Where was Joseph taken?","a":"Egypt","b":"Babylon","c":"Rome","correct":"a"},{"q":"What did Joseph do when his brothers came?","a":"He sent them away","b":"He forgave them","c":"He hid from them","correct":"b"}],"steps":["Jacob gave Joseph a colourful coat","Joseph's brothers sold him","Joseph explained Pharaoh's dreams","Joseph forgave his brothers"],"verse":"But as for you, ye thought evil against me; but God meant it unto good.","verseRef":"Genesis 50:20","missing":"good","prayer":"Dear God, help me to forgive others, like Joseph forgave his brothers. Thank You that You can bring good out of hard times. Amen.","lesson":"God can turn bad things into good, and I can choose to forgive."},{"slug":"red-sea","title":"Moses and the Red Sea","icon":"🌊","image":"","discover":"God's people were slaves in Egypt. God chose Moses to lead them to freedom, and then He did something amazing at the sea.","story":"\u003Cp\u003EGod's people worked very hard as slaves in Egypt. God spoke to Moses from a burning bush and sent him to tell Pharaoh, “Let my people go!”\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EAt last Pharaoh let them go, and God's people left Egypt. God led them with a pillar of cloud by day and a pillar of fire by night.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EBut Pharaoh changed his mind and chased them with his army. God's people were stuck between the soldiers and the Red Sea!\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EMoses lifted his staff, and God sent a strong wind. The waters parted, and the people walked across on dry ground. God had saved them!\u003C/p\u003E\n","refLabel":"Exodus 14","bibleUrl":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/read/eng-kjv/Exodus/14/1","audio":"","quiz":[{"q":"Who did God send to speak to Pharaoh?","a":"Moses","b":"Noah","c":"David","correct":"a"},{"q":"How did God lead the people at night?","a":"With a lantern","b":"With a pillar of fire","c":"With a bright moon","correct":"b"},{"q":"What happened to the Red Sea?","a":"It froze","b":"The waters parted","c":"It dried up for a year","correct":"b"}],"steps":["God spoke to Moses from a burning bush","Pharaoh let the people go","Pharaoh's army chased them","God parted the Red Sea"],"verse":"The LORD shall fight for you, and ye shall hold your peace.","verseRef":"Exodus 14:14","missing":"fight","prayer":"Dear God, thank You for saving Your people. When I feel stuck, help me to remember that You can make a way. Amen.","lesson":"God can make a way when there seems to be no way."},{"slug":"jonah","title":"Jonah and the Great Fish","icon":"🐋","image":"","discover":"God asked Jonah to go to the city of Nineveh, but Jonah ran the other way. God did not give up on Jonah, or on Nineveh.","story":"\u003Cp\u003EGod said to Jonah, “Go to Nineveh and tell the people to stop doing wrong.” But Jonah did not want to go, so he got on a ship going far away.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EGod sent a great storm. The sailors were terrified. Jonah said, “This is my fault. Throw me into the sea.”\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EGod sent a great fish to swallow Jonah. For three days and nights Jonah prayed inside the fish, and then the fish spat him out onto dry land.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThis time Jonah obeyed. The people of Nineveh listened, said sorry to God, and God forgave them.\u003C/p\u003E\n","refLabel":"Jonah 1 to 3","bibleUrl":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/read/eng-kjv/Jonah/1/1","audio":"","quiz":[{"q":"Where did God ask Jonah to go?","a":"Nineveh","b":"Egypt","c":"Jerusalem","correct":"a"},{"q":"What swallowed Jonah?","a":"A shark","b":"A great fish","c":"A whale's baby","correct":"b"},{"q":"What did the people of Nineveh do?","a":"They laughed","b":"They said sorry to God","c":"They ran away","correct":"b"}],"steps":["God asked Jonah to go to Nineveh","Jonah ran away on a ship","A great fish swallowed Jonah","The people of Nineveh said sorry"],"verse":"Salvation is of the LORD.","verseRef":"Jonah 2:9","missing":"Salvation","prayer":"Dear God, help me to listen and obey when You ask me to do something. Thank You for giving second chances. Amen.","lesson":"God gives second chances, and I should listen to Him."},{"slug":"daniel-lions","title":"Daniel in the Lions’ Den","icon":"🦁","image":"","discover":"Daniel loved God and prayed to Him every day. When a law said he must stop praying, Daniel kept praying anyway.","story":"\u003Cp\u003EDaniel was a wise man who served the king. Three times every day, he knelt by his window and prayed to God.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003ESome jealous men tricked the king into making a law: for thirty days, nobody could pray to anyone but the king.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EDaniel kept praying to God. So he was thrown into a den of hungry lions!\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe king could not sleep all night. In the morning he ran to the den. Daniel called out, “My God sent His angel and shut the lions' mouths!”\u003C/p\u003E\n","refLabel":"Daniel 6","bibleUrl":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/read/eng-kjv/Daniel/6/1","audio":"","quiz":[{"q":"How many times a day did Daniel pray?","a":"Once","b":"Three times","c":"Ten times","correct":"b"},{"q":"Where was Daniel thrown?","a":"A lions' den","b":"A deep well","c":"A dark cave","correct":"a"},{"q":"Who shut the lions' mouths?","a":"The king","b":"God's angel","c":"The guards","correct":"b"}],"steps":["Daniel prayed three times a day","A law said no one could pray to God","Daniel was thrown to the lions","God's angel shut the lions' mouths"],"verse":"My God hath sent his angel, and hath shut the lions' mouths.","verseRef":"Daniel 6:22","missing":"angel","prayer":"Dear God, help me to talk to You every day, like Daniel. Keep me brave and faithful. Amen.","lesson":"I can pray to God every day, and He protects me."}]},{"key":"jesus","name":"☦ Jesus Trail","stops":[{"slug":"birth-of-jesus","title":"The Birth of Jesus","icon":"⭐","image":"","discover":"God made a wonderful promise: He would send a Saviour. One night, in the little town of Bethlehem, that promise came true. Jesus was born!","story":"\u003Cp\u003EThe Virgin Mary and Joseph travelled a long way to the town of Bethlehem. The town was so full that there was no room for them to stay.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThat night, Jesus was born. Mary wrapped Him in cloth and laid Him in a manger, where the animals ate their food.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EOut in the fields, shepherds were watching their sheep. Suddenly an angel appeared and said, \"Do not be afraid! I bring you good news of great joy. A Saviour has been born, Christ the Lord!\"\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThen many angels filled the sky, singing \"Glory to God in the highest!\" The shepherds hurried to Bethlehem, found baby Jesus, and told everyone the good news.\u003C/p\u003E\n","refLabel":"Luke 2","bibleUrl":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/read/eng-kjv/Luke/2/1","audio":"","quiz":[{"q":"Where was Jesus born?","a":"Bethlehem","b":"Rome","c":"Egypt","correct":"a"},{"q":"Where did Mary lay baby Jesus?","a":"In a boat","b":"In a manger","c":"In a palace bed","correct":"b"},{"q":"Who told the shepherds the good news?","a":"A king","b":"A fisherman","c":"The angels","correct":"c"}],"steps":["Mary and Joseph travelled to Bethlehem","Jesus was born and laid in a manger","Angels told the shepherds the good news","The shepherds came to see baby Jesus"],"verse":"For unto you is born this day in the city of David a Saviour, which is Christ the Lord.","verseRef":"Luke 2:11","missing":"Saviour","prayer":"Thank You, God, for sending Jesus to be our Saviour. Help me to share the good news with joy, like the shepherds did. Amen.","lesson":"Jesus came to save us because God loves us."},{"slug":"resurrection","title":"Christ Is Risen!","icon":"☦","image":"","discover":"Jesus died on the cross for us, and His friends were very sad. But on the third day, something amazing happened. Christ is risen!","story":"\u003Cp\u003EVery early on Sunday morning, some women who loved Jesus went to His tomb. They were carrying sweet-smelling spices.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWhen they arrived, the big stone had been rolled away! An angel in shining white was sitting there.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe angel said, \"Do not be afraid. Jesus is not here. He is risen, just as He said!\"\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe women ran with great joy to tell Jesus' friends, and on the way Jesus Himself met them. Jesus is alive! That is why we say with joy: \"Christ is risen!\" and answer, \"Truly He is risen!\"\u003C/p\u003E\n","refLabel":"Matthew 28","bibleUrl":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/read/eng-kjv/Matthew/28/1","audio":"","quiz":[{"q":"Who was waiting at the tomb?","a":"An angel","b":"A shepherd","c":"A king","correct":"a"},{"q":"On which day did Jesus rise?","a":"The first day","b":"The third day","c":"The tenth day","correct":"b"},{"q":"What did the angel say?","a":"He is sleeping","b":"He is risen","c":"He went fishing","correct":"b"}],"steps":["The women came to the tomb early in the morning","They saw the stone rolled away","The angel said, \"He is risen!\"","The women ran to tell Jesus' friends"],"verse":"He is not here: for he is risen, as he said.","verseRef":"Matthew 28:6","missing":"risen","prayer":"Thank You, Jesus, for loving me so much and for rising from the dead. Help me to live with joy, because You are alive. Amen.","lesson":"Jesus is alive, and He is always with me."},{"slug":"baptism-of-jesus","title":"The Baptism of Jesus","icon":"🕊","image":"","discover":"When Jesus was grown up, He came to the River Jordan to be baptised by John. Something wonderful happened that showed us who God is.","story":"\u003Cp\u003EJohn the Baptist was baptising people in the River Jordan and telling them to get ready for the Saviour.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EOne day Jesus came to be baptised. John said, “I need to be baptised by You!” But Jesus asked him to go ahead.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EAs Jesus came up out of the water, the heavens opened and the Holy Spirit came down like a dove.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EA voice from heaven said, “This is my beloved Son.” The Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit were shown together. We remember this at the feast of Theophany.\u003C/p\u003E\n","refLabel":"Matthew 3","bibleUrl":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/read/eng-kjv/Matthew/3/13","audio":"","quiz":[{"q":"Where was Jesus baptised?","a":"The River Jordan","b":"The Red Sea","c":"A well","correct":"a"},{"q":"How did the Holy Spirit come down?","a":"Like fire","b":"Like a dove","c":"Like rain","correct":"b"},{"q":"What feast remembers Jesus' Baptism?","a":"Theophany","b":"Pascha","c":"Christmas","correct":"a"}],"steps":["John baptised people in the river","Jesus came to be baptised","The Holy Spirit came down like a dove","A voice said, “This is my beloved Son”"],"verse":"This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.","verseRef":"Matthew 3:17","missing":"beloved","prayer":"Holy Trinity, Father, Son and Holy Spirit, thank You for my baptism. Help me to live as a child of God. Amen.","lesson":"At Theophany we see the Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit."},{"slug":"calming-the-storm","title":"Jesus Calms the Storm","icon":"⛵","image":"","discover":"Jesus and His friends were crossing the lake in a boat when a huge storm came. The friends were terrified, but Jesus was fast asleep.","story":"\u003Cp\u003EOne evening Jesus said to His disciples, “Let us go across the lake.” They got into a boat, and Jesus fell asleep.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003ESuddenly a great storm blew. Waves crashed into the boat, and it began to fill with water!\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe disciples woke Jesus. “Teacher, don't You care that we are sinking?”\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EJesus stood up and said to the wind and the waves, “Peace, be still.” At once everything was calm. The disciples said, “Even the wind and the sea obey Him!”\u003C/p\u003E\n","refLabel":"Mark 4","bibleUrl":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/read/eng-kjv/Mark/4/35","audio":"","quiz":[{"q":"What was Jesus doing when the storm came?","a":"Fishing","b":"Sleeping","c":"Eating","correct":"b"},{"q":"What did Jesus say to the storm?","a":"Go away","b":"Peace, be still","c":"Stop now","correct":"b"},{"q":"What obeyed Jesus?","a":"The wind and the sea","b":"Only the fish","c":"The boat","correct":"a"}],"steps":["Jesus and His friends got into a boat","Jesus fell asleep","A great storm came","Jesus calmed the wind and the waves"],"verse":"Peace, be still.","verseRef":"Mark 4:39","missing":"Peace","prayer":"Jesus, when I feel scared, please calm the storm in my heart and fill me with Your peace. Amen.","lesson":"Jesus is stronger than any storm."},{"slug":"feeding-five-thousand","title":"Jesus Feeds Five Thousand","icon":"🍞","image":"","discover":"A huge crowd followed Jesus to listen to Him. When everyone grew hungry, a boy shared his small lunch, and Jesus did something amazing.","story":"\u003Cp\u003EThousands of people came to hear Jesus teach. As evening came, they were hungry, but there was nowhere to buy food.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EA boy had five small loaves of bread and two fish. He gave them to Jesus.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EJesus looked up to heaven, gave thanks and broke the bread. The disciples shared it with everyone.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EAll five thousand people ate until they were full, and there were twelve baskets of food left over!\u003C/p\u003E\n","refLabel":"John 6","bibleUrl":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/read/eng-kjv/John/6/1","audio":"","quiz":[{"q":"What did the boy share?","a":"Five loaves and two fish","b":"Ten apples","c":"A big cake","correct":"a"},{"q":"What did Jesus do before sharing the food?","a":"He gave thanks","b":"He sang a song","c":"He asked for money","correct":"a"},{"q":"How many baskets were left over?","a":"Two","b":"Seven","c":"Twelve","correct":"c"}],"steps":["A big crowd came to hear Jesus","A boy gave his loaves and fish","Jesus gave thanks and broke the bread","Everyone ate and there were leftovers"],"verse":"I am the bread of life.","verseRef":"John 6:35","missing":"bread","prayer":"Thank You, Jesus, for giving us everything we need. Help me to share what I have, like the boy with the loaves and fish. Amen.","lesson":"When I share, God can do great things."},{"slug":"lost-sheep","title":"The Lost Sheep","icon":"🐑","image":"","discover":"Jesus told a story about a shepherd who had a hundred sheep. When one sheep got lost, the shepherd went looking for it.","story":"\u003Cp\u003EA shepherd had one hundred sheep. He knew each one and cared for them all.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EOne day he counted them and found only ninety-nine. One little sheep was lost!\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe shepherd left the ninety-nine safe and searched everywhere until he found the lost sheep. He carried it home on his shoulders.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EHe called his friends and said, “Rejoice with me; I have found my lost sheep!” Jesus said heaven rejoices like this when one person comes back to God.\u003C/p\u003E\n","refLabel":"Luke 15","bibleUrl":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/read/eng-kjv/Luke/15/1","audio":"","quiz":[{"q":"How many sheep did the shepherd have?","a":"Ten","b":"One hundred","c":"Fifty","correct":"b"},{"q":"What did the shepherd do?","a":"He forgot the lost sheep","b":"He searched until he found it","c":"He bought a new sheep","correct":"b"},{"q":"How did he carry the sheep home?","a":"On his shoulders","b":"In a basket","c":"In a cart","correct":"a"}],"steps":["The shepherd counted his sheep","One sheep was lost","The shepherd searched and found it","He carried it home rejoicing"],"verse":"Rejoice with me; for I have found my sheep which was lost.","verseRef":"Luke 15:6","missing":"found","prayer":"Jesus, my Good Shepherd, thank You that You always look for me and never give up on me. Amen.","lesson":"Jesus is my Good Shepherd, and every person matters to Him."},{"slug":"zacchaeus","title":"Zacchaeus Meets Jesus","icon":"🌳","image":"","discover":"Zacchaeus was a rich tax collector, and he was very short. He wanted to see Jesus so much that he climbed a tree!","story":"\u003Cp\u003EZacchaeus collected taxes in Jericho, and he often took more money than he should. People did not like him.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWhen Jesus came to town, a big crowd gathered. Zacchaeus was too short to see, so he ran ahead and climbed a sycamore tree.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EJesus stopped under the tree, looked up and said, “Zacchaeus, come down! I am coming to your house today.”\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EZacchaeus was so happy. He said, “I will give half of what I have to the poor, and pay back four times what I took.” Jesus had changed his heart.\u003C/p\u003E\n","refLabel":"Luke 19","bibleUrl":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/read/eng-kjv/Luke/19/1","audio":"","quiz":[{"q":"Why did Zacchaeus climb a tree?","a":"To pick fruit","b":"He was too short to see Jesus","c":"To hide","correct":"b"},{"q":"Where did Jesus go?","a":"To Zacchaeus' house","b":"To the temple","c":"To the sea","correct":"a"},{"q":"What did Zacchaeus promise?","a":"To give to the poor","b":"To buy a new house","c":"To leave town","correct":"a"}],"steps":["Zacchaeus wanted to see Jesus","He climbed a sycamore tree","Jesus said, “Come down!”","Zacchaeus promised to give to the poor"],"verse":"For the Son of man is come to seek and to save that which was lost.","verseRef":"Luke 19:10","missing":"seek","prayer":"Jesus, thank You for loving everyone. Change my heart like You changed Zacchaeus' heart, and help me to be generous. Amen.","lesson":"Jesus loves everyone, and He can change hearts."}]},{"key":"saints","name":"🕯 Saints Trail","stops":[{"slug":"saint-nicholas","title":"Saint Nicholas","icon":"🎁","image":"","discover":"Long ago there lived a kind bishop called Nicholas. He loved Jesus so much that he loved to help people in need, and he did it quietly, without wanting any praise.","story":"\u003Cp\u003ENicholas lived a long time ago in a town called Myra. When he grew up, he became a bishop, a shepherd of God's people, caring for the church there.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003ENicholas heard about a poor father who had three daughters. The family had no money at all, and they were very worried.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003ESo one night, Nicholas quietly went to their house and dropped a bag of gold through the window. He did not want anyone to know it was him. He did it again, and again, until each daughter had been helped.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003ENicholas remembered what Jesus taught: when you give, do it in secret, and your Father in heaven will see. The Church remembers Saint Nicholas every year on 6 December, and his kindness still teaches us to share with joy.\u003C/p\u003E\n","refLabel":"Matthew 6","bibleUrl":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/read/eng-kjv/Matthew/6/1","audio":"","quiz":[{"q":"What was Nicholas's job?","a":"A bishop","b":"A soldier","c":"A fisherman","correct":"a"},{"q":"What did Nicholas give to the poor family?","a":"A new house","b":"Bags of gold","c":"A big boat","correct":"b"},{"q":"How did Nicholas give his gifts?","a":"With a loud trumpet","b":"In secret","c":"Only to his friends","correct":"b"}],"steps":["Nicholas became a bishop in Myra","He heard about a poor family","He secretly dropped gold through the window","The family was helped and thanked God"],"verse":"It is more blessed to give than to receive.","verseRef":"Acts 20:35","missing":"give","prayer":"Holy Saint Nicholas, pray for us. Dear Jesus, help me to be kind and generous like Saint Nicholas, and to share what I have with joy. Amen.","lesson":"I can share and be kind, even when nobody sees."},{"slug":"saint-george","title":"Saint George","icon":"🛡","image":"","discover":"George was a brave soldier who loved Jesus. When he was told to stop following Jesus, George chose to stay faithful, no matter what.","story":"\u003Cp\u003EGeorge was a soldier in the army of a great emperor long ago. He was strong and brave, and everyone knew he was a Christian.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EOne day the emperor made a law against Christians. Everyone had to stop following Jesus. Many people were afraid.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EBut George was not ashamed of Jesus. He stood up and said, \"I am a Christian.\" He gave away what he owned to the poor and told everyone about God's love.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe emperor was very angry, but George stayed faithful to Jesus to the very end. That is why the Church calls him a Great Martyr. Icons often show him on a horse defeating a dragon, a picture of good defeating evil with God's help.\u003C/p\u003E\n","refLabel":"Ephesians 6","bibleUrl":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/read/eng-kjv/Ephesians/6/10","audio":"","quiz":[{"q":"What was George's job?","a":"A shepherd","b":"A soldier","c":"A baker","correct":"b"},{"q":"What did George do when he was told to stop following Jesus?","a":"He stayed faithful to Jesus","b":"He ran away","c":"He hid in a cave","correct":"a"},{"q":"What do icons of Saint George often show him defeating?","a":"A giant","b":"A dragon","c":"A lion","correct":"b"}],"steps":["George served as a soldier","The emperor made a law against Christians","George said, \"I am a Christian\"","George stayed faithful to Jesus to the end"],"verse":"Be strong and of a good courage; be not afraid, neither be thou dismayed: for the LORD thy God is with thee whithersoever thou goest.","verseRef":"Joshua 1:9","missing":"courage","prayer":"Holy Saint George, pray for us. Dear Jesus, make me brave like Saint George, so I am never ashamed to love You. Amen.","lesson":"God makes me brave to follow Jesus."},{"slug":"saint-spyridon","title":"Saint Spyridon","icon":"🐑","image":"","discover":"Spyridon was a humble shepherd on the island of Cyprus. He loved God so much that he became a bishop, but he never stopped caring for his sheep, or for people.","story":"\u003Cp\u003ESpyridon was a shepherd who lived simply and shared everything he had with people in need.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EBecause he was so kind and faithful, the people chose him to be their bishop. Even then, he still wore simple clothes and cared for his sheep.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EAt a great council of bishops, someone asked how God can be One and yet Three. Spyridon picked up a clay brick and squeezed it. The Church remembers that fire rose up, water ran down, and clay stayed in his hand: three things in one brick.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003ESaint Spyridon's relics rest on the island of Corfu, and Christians around the world ask for his prayers.\u003C/p\u003E\n","refLabel":"Psalm 23","bibleUrl":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/read/eng-kjv/Psalms/23/1","audio":"","quiz":[{"q":"What was Spyridon's work before he was a bishop?","a":"Shepherd","b":"Soldier","c":"Sailor","correct":"a"},{"q":"On which island did he live?","a":"Cyprus","b":"Crete","c":"Sicily","correct":"a"},{"q":"What did he use to explain the Holy Trinity?","a":"A brick","b":"A candle","c":"A flower","correct":"a"}],"steps":["Spyridon was a kind shepherd","He was chosen to be a bishop","He explained the Trinity with a brick","His relics rest on Corfu"],"verse":"The LORD is my shepherd; I shall not want.","verseRef":"Psalm 23:1","missing":"shepherd","prayer":"Holy Saint Spyridon, pray for us. Dear God, help me to be humble and kind, and to share what I have. Amen.","lesson":"Being humble and kind is what makes someone great in God's eyes."}]}]}</script></div></section><section id="verse-garden" class="kjt-trail kjt-kids kjt-kids--garden" aria-labelledby="verse-garden-heading"><div class="kjt-trail__wrap"><div class="kk-banner kk-banner--light" style="--kb1:#3F9B4C;--kb2:#8BD18F"><span class="kk-banner__badge" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-core/assets/kids-extras/cards/garden.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><div class="kk-banner__text"><p class="kjt-trail__eyebrow">Kids Corner · Remember</p><h2 id="verse-garden-heading" class="kjt-trail__title">Memory Verse Garden</h2><p class="kjt-trail__intro">Every time you finish a stop on the Adventure Trail, a new flower grows here. Tap a flower to practise its memory verse.</p></div></div><div class="kk-app" data-kjt-garden><p class="kt-note">Finish a stop on the Bible Adventure Trail to plant your first flower.</p></div></div></section><section id="prayer-garden" class="kjt-trail kjt-kids kjt-kids--prayer" aria-labelledby="prayer-garden-heading"><div class="kjt-trail__wrap"><div class="kk-banner kk-banner--light" style="--kb1:#3B3F8F;--kb2:#7A5BB5"><span class="kk-banner__badge" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-core/assets/kids-extras/cards/prayer.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><div class="kk-banner__text"><p class="kjt-trail__eyebrow">Kids Corner · Pray</p><h2 id="prayer-garden-heading" class="kjt-trail__title">Prayer Garden</h2><p class="kjt-trail__intro">How do you feel today? Tap a button, and pray with Jesus. He is always listening.</p></div></div><div class="kk-app" data-kjt-prayer><div class="kk-feelings"><button type="button" class="kk-feel" data-prayer="0" aria-expanded="false"><span class="kk-feel__icon" aria-hidden="true">💛</span><span class="kk-feel__label">Thank you, Jesus</span></button><button type="button" class="kk-feel" data-prayer="1" aria-expanded="false"><span class="kk-feel__icon" aria-hidden="true">😢</span><span class="kk-feel__label">I feel sad</span></button><button type="button" class="kk-feel" data-prayer="2" aria-expanded="false"><span class="kk-feel__icon" aria-hidden="true">😨</span><span class="kk-feel__label">I feel afraid</span></button><button type="button" class="kk-feel" data-prayer="3" aria-expanded="false"><span class="kk-feel__icon" aria-hidden="true">🙏</span><span class="kk-feel__label">I need help</span></button><button type="button" class="kk-feel" data-prayer="4" aria-expanded="false"><span class="kk-feel__icon" aria-hidden="true">👨‍👩‍👧</span><span class="kk-feel__label">Pray for my family</span></button><button type="button" class="kk-feel" data-prayer="5" aria-expanded="false"><span class="kk-feel__icon" aria-hidden="true">🌙</span><span class="kk-feel__label">Bedtime</span></button><button type="button" class="kk-feel" data-prayer="6" aria-expanded="false"><span class="kk-feel__icon" aria-hidden="true">☀️</span><span class="kk-feel__label">Good morning</span></button><button type="button" class="kk-feel" data-prayer="7" aria-expanded="false"><span class="kk-feel__icon" aria-hidden="true">🍞</span><span class="kk-feel__label">Before meals</span></button><button type="button" class="kk-feel" data-prayer="8" aria-expanded="false"><span class="kk-feel__icon" aria-hidden="true">🎒</span><span class="kk-feel__label">Before school</span></button><button type="button" class="kk-feel" data-prayer="9" aria-expanded="false"><span class="kk-feel__icon" aria-hidden="true">🤗</span><span class="kk-feel__label">I feel happy</span></button><button type="button" class="kk-feel" data-prayer="10" aria-expanded="false"><span class="kk-feel__icon" aria-hidden="true">🥺</span><span class="kk-feel__label">I feel lonely</span></button><button type="button" class="kk-feel" data-prayer="11" aria-expanded="false"><span class="kk-feel__icon" aria-hidden="true">😔</span><span class="kk-feel__label">I&#039;m sorry</span></button><button type="button" class="kk-feel" data-prayer="12" aria-expanded="false"><span class="kk-feel__icon" aria-hidden="true">🤒</span><span class="kk-feel__label">For someone who is sick</span></button><button type="button" class="kk-feel" data-prayer="13" aria-expanded="false"><span class="kk-feel__icon" aria-hidden="true">🤝</span><span class="kk-feel__label">For my friends</span></button><button type="button" class="kk-feel" data-prayer="14" aria-expanded="false"><span class="kk-feel__icon" aria-hidden="true">☦</span><span class="kk-feel__label">The Jesus Prayer</span></button><button type="button" class="kk-feel" data-prayer="15" aria-expanded="false"><span class="kk-feel__icon" aria-hidden="true">☦</span><span class="kk-feel__label">The Lord&#039;s Prayer</span></button></div><div class="kk-prayers" aria-live="polite"><div class="kk-prayer" data-prayer-card="0" hidden><p class="kk-prayer__title">💛 Thank you, Jesus</p><p class="kk-prayer__text">Thank You, Jesus, for this day, for my family, for my food and for Your love. Everything good comes from You. Glory to God for all things! Amen.</p><p class="kk-prayer__text" hidden>Dear Lord, thank You for the sun, the rain, the trees and the animals, and thank You for making me. Help me to say thank You every day. Amen.</p><p class="kk-prayer__text" hidden>Thank You, God, for my friends and the people who love me. Thank You that You are always with me. Amen.</p></div><div class="kk-prayer" data-prayer-card="1" hidden><p class="kk-prayer__title">😢 I feel sad</p><p class="kk-prayer__text">Dear Jesus, I feel sad today. Please hold me close and comfort my heart. Help me remember that You are always with me and You love me. Amen.</p><p class="kk-prayer__text" hidden>Lord Jesus, You cried when Your friend Lazarus died, so You know how sadness feels. Please be near me and give me Your peace. Amen.</p><p class="kk-prayer__text" hidden>Dear God, my heart feels heavy. Please send someone kind to help me, and help me to tell a grown-up how I feel. Amen.</p></div><div class="kk-prayer" data-prayer-card="2" hidden><p class="kk-prayer__title">😨 I feel afraid</p><p class="kk-prayer__text">Lord Jesus, I feel afraid. Please be with me and keep me safe. Send Your holy angel to guard me, and help me to trust You. Amen.</p><p class="kk-prayer__text" hidden>Dear God, when David was afraid, he trusted You. Help me to be brave like him, because You are with me. Amen.</p><p class="kk-prayer__text" hidden>Jesus, You calmed the storm with a word. Please calm the storm inside me and fill me with peace. Amen.</p></div><div class="kk-prayer" data-prayer-card="3" hidden><p class="kk-prayer__title">🙏 I need help</p><p class="kk-prayer__text">Dear God, I need Your help. You know everything and You can do anything. Please show me what to do, and help me to be patient and kind. Amen.</p><p class="kk-prayer__text" hidden>Lord, please help me with the things that feel too hard today. Give me a clear mind and a calm heart. Amen.</p></div><div class="kk-prayer" data-prayer-card="4" hidden><p class="kk-prayer__title">👨‍👩‍👧 Pray for my family</p><p class="kk-prayer__text">Lord Jesus, please bless my family. Keep us safe, help us to love and forgive each other, and be with everyone I love today. Amen.</p><p class="kk-prayer__text" hidden>Dear God, thank You for my family. Please give us kind words, happy hearts and peace in our home. Amen.</p></div><div class="kk-prayer" data-prayer-card="5" hidden><p class="kk-prayer__title">🌙 Bedtime</p><p class="kk-prayer__text">Lord Jesus, thank You for today. Forgive me for anything wrong I did. Watch over me while I sleep, and send Your angel to guard me through the night. Amen.</p><p class="kk-prayer__text" hidden>Into Your hands, O Lord, I give my body and my soul. Bless me and keep me through this night. Amen.</p><p class="kk-prayer__text" hidden>Good night, dear Jesus. Thank You for being with me all day. Please give me peaceful sleep and happy dreams. Amen.</p></div><div class="kk-prayer" data-prayer-card="6" hidden><p class="kk-prayer__title">☀️ Good morning</p><p class="kk-prayer__text">Glory to You, O God, for this new day! Help me to love You and to be kind to everyone I meet today. Amen.</p><p class="kk-prayer__text" hidden>Good morning, Lord! Thank You for waking me up. Be with me in everything I do and say today. Amen.</p></div><div class="kk-prayer" data-prayer-card="7" hidden><p class="kk-prayer__title">🍞 Before meals</p><p class="kk-prayer__text">Bless, O Lord, this food and those who made it, and give bread to those who are hungry. Amen.</p><p class="kk-prayer__text" hidden>Thank You, God, for this food. Help it make us strong so we can serve You and help others. Amen.</p></div><div class="kk-prayer" data-prayer-card="8" hidden><p class="kk-prayer__title">🎒 Before school</p><p class="kk-prayer__text">Dear God, please be with me at school today. Help me to listen, to learn, and to be a good friend. Amen.</p><p class="kk-prayer__text" hidden>Lord, give me wisdom like Solomon and courage like David for everything I learn today. Amen.</p></div><div class="kk-prayer" data-prayer-card="9" hidden><p class="kk-prayer__title">🤗 I feel happy</p><p class="kk-prayer__text">Thank You, Lord, for my happy heart! Everything good comes from You. Help me to share this joy with others. Amen.</p><p class="kk-prayer__text" hidden>Glory to God! I am so happy today. Thank You, Jesus, for Your love that makes my heart sing. Amen.</p></div><div class="kk-prayer" data-prayer-card="10" hidden><p class="kk-prayer__title">🥺 I feel lonely</p><p class="kk-prayer__text">Dear Jesus, I feel alone. Please remind me that You are always my friend, and help me to find good friends too. Amen.</p><p class="kk-prayer__text" hidden>Lord, You never leave me. When I feel lonely, fill my heart with Your love and bring kind people near me. Amen.</p></div><div class="kk-prayer" data-prayer-card="11" hidden><p class="kk-prayer__title">😔 I&#039;m sorry</p><p class="kk-prayer__text">Dear God, I am sorry for what I did wrong. Please forgive me, and help me to make it right and do better. Amen.</p><p class="kk-prayer__text" hidden>Lord Jesus, have mercy on me. Help me to say sorry to the people I have hurt, and to forgive others too. Amen.</p></div><div class="kk-prayer" data-prayer-card="12" hidden><p class="kk-prayer__title">🤒 For someone who is sick</p><p class="kk-prayer__text">Lord Jesus, You healed so many people. Please be with those who are sick today, and help them to get well. Amen.</p><p class="kk-prayer__text" hidden>Dear God, please comfort and heal everyone who is ill, and bless the doctors and nurses who care for them. Amen.</p></div><div class="kk-prayer" data-prayer-card="13" hidden><p class="kk-prayer__title">🤝 For my friends</p><p class="kk-prayer__text">Dear Jesus, please bless my friends. Keep them safe and happy, and help us to be kind to each other. Amen.</p></div><div class="kk-prayer" data-prayer-card="14" hidden><p class="kk-prayer__title">☦ The Jesus Prayer</p><p class="kk-prayer__text">Lord Jesus Christ, Son of God, have mercy on me. (Christians have prayed these words for hundreds of years. You can say them slowly, anytime and anywhere.)</p></div><div class="kk-prayer" data-prayer-card="15" hidden><p class="kk-prayer__title">☦ The Lord&#039;s Prayer</p><p class="kk-prayer__text">Our Father, who art in heaven, hallowed be Thy name. Thy kingdom come, Thy will be done, on earth as it is in heaven. Give us this day our daily bread, and forgive us our trespasses, as we forgive those who trespass against us. And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from the evil one. Amen.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section id="story-adventures" class="kjt-trail kjt-kids kjt-kids--stories" aria-labelledby="story-adventures-heading"><div class="kjt-trail__wrap"><div class="kk-banner kk-banner--light" style="--kb1:#8D5A2B;--kb2:#D9A05B"><span class="kk-banner__badge" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-core/assets/kids-extras/cards/stories.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><div class="kk-banner__text"><p class="kjt-trail__eyebrow">Kids Corner · Read &amp; Choose</p><h2 id="story-adventures-heading" class="kjt-trail__title">Story Adventures</h2><p class="kjt-trail__intro">You choose what happens next! Walk through Bible stories, travel with the saints, and decide what you would do.</p></div></div><div class="kad-card"><img class="kad-card__bg" src="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/kids-adventure/img/bg-camp.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><div class="kad-card__chars" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/kids-adventure/img/david.webp" alt="" loading="lazy"><img src="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/kids-adventure/img/goliath.webp" alt="" loading="lazy"></div><div class="kad-card__body"><span class="kad-card__new">New &middot; Bible adventure</span><h3>David &amp; Goliath</h3><p>Be the shepherd boy who trusted God. Find the lost lambs, play your harp, meet the prophet Samuel, choose five smooth stones, and face the giant.</p><button type="button" class="kad-card__go" data-kjt-adventure="david">&#9654; Start the adventure</button><p class="kad-card__progress" data-kjt-adventure-progress="david">7 chapters &middot; about 25 minutes</p></div></div><div class="kad-card kad-card--armour"><img class="kad-card__bg" src="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/kids-adventure/img/armour/bg-battle.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><div class="kad-card__chars" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/kids-adventure/img/armour/card-hero.webp" alt="" loading="lazy"><img src="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/kids-adventure/img/armour/devil.webp" alt="" loading="lazy"></div><div class="kad-card__body"><span class="kad-card__new">New &middot; Bible adventure</span><h3>The Armour of God</h3><p>You start small, weak and afraid. Win the seven pieces of the armour of God in seven missions, then stand against the devil himself. Without the whole armour, nobody can stand!</p><button type="button" class="kad-card__go" data-kjt-adventure="armour">&#9654; Start the adventure</button><p class="kad-card__progress" data-kjt-adventure-progress="armour">8 chapters &middot; about 30 minutes</p></div></div><div class="ks-app" data-kjt-stories><p class="kt-note">The stories need JavaScript turned on.</p></div><script type="application/json" id="kjt-stories-data">{"stories":[{"id":"shepherds-night","category":"bible","icon":"⭐","title":"The Shepherds' Night","summary":"It is a quiet night on the hills near Bethlehem, until the sky fills with light.","passage":{"label":"Luke 2","book":"Luke","chapter":2,"verse":8},"scenes":{"start":{"text":"You are a young shepherd on the hills near Bethlehem. The night is cold and dark. Your father and the other shepherds sit around a small fire, keeping watch over the sheep. Suddenly you notice that one little lamb has wandered away into the darkness.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"hills","props":[["sheep",18,86,1],["sheep",30,90,0.9],["fire",55,90,1.1],["person",62,90,1,"#8d6e63"],["person",72,90,1,"#6d4c41"],["child",45,90,1,"#a1887f"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Go after the lost lamb","to":"lamb"},{"text":"Stay by the warm fire","to":"fire"}]},"lamb":{"text":"You pick up your staff and follow the soft bleating. Behind some rocks you find the little lamb, shivering. You lift it gently into your arms. “There you are,” you whisper. As you turn back towards the fire, the whole sky begins to glow.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"hills","props":[["rocks",40,90,1.2],["child",55,90,1.1,"#a1887f"],["sheep",62,86,0.6]]},"choices":[{"text":"Look up","to":"angel"}]},"fire":{"text":"You stay by the fire. Your grandfather pokes the embers and tells an old story: long ago, the prophets promised that a Saviour would come, and that he would be born right here, in little Bethlehem. “One day,” he says, “God will keep His promise.” Then, all at once, the night becomes bright as day.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"hills","props":[["fire",50,90,1.2],["person",38,90,1,"#6d4c41"],["child",62,90,1,"#a1887f"],["sheep",82,88,0.9]]},"choices":[{"text":"Look up","to":"angel"}]},"angel":{"text":"An angel of the Lord stands before you, and the glory of the Lord shines all around. Everyone is terribly afraid. But the angel says, “Fear not: for, behold, I bring you good tidings of great joy, which shall be to all people. For unto you is born this day in the city of David a Saviour, which is Christ the Lord.” Then the sky is filled with angels singing, “Glory to God in the highest!”","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"hills","props":[["angel",50,55,1.6],["angel",20,40,0.8],["angel",80,38,0.8],["person",35,92,0.9,"#6d4c41"],["child",62,92,0.9,"#a1887f"],["sheep",78,90,0.8]]},"choices":[{"text":"Hide behind your father","to":"hide"},{"text":"Listen with wonder","to":"wonder"}]},"hide":{"text":"You hide behind your father's cloak, your heart pounding. But your father holds your hand and smiles. “Don't be afraid,” he says. “Did you hear? The angel said it is good news, news of great joy, for everyone. Even for shepherds like us.”","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"hills","props":[["light",50,45,1.2],["person",45,92,1.2,"#6d4c41"],["child",56,92,0.9,"#a1887f"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Go with the shepherds","to":"go"}]},"wonder":{"text":"You stand very still, listening to the most beautiful song you have ever heard. The Saviour, the one Grandfather talked about, has been born tonight! Your heart feels so full of joy that you could burst.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"hills","props":[["light",50,45,1.4],["child",50,92,1.1,"#a1887f"],["sheep",30,90,0.8]]},"choices":[{"text":"Go with the shepherds","to":"go"}]},"go":{"text":"When the angels go back into heaven, the shepherds say to one another, “Let us now go even unto Bethlehem, and see this thing which is come to pass.” Everyone hurries down the hill towards the little town.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"street","props":[["star",62,18,1.4],["town",50,82,1],["person",25,92,0.9,"#6d4c41"],["child",35,92,0.8,"#a1887f"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Bring a lamb as a gift","to":"gift"},{"text":"Run ahead to find the way","to":"run"},{"text":"Stay behind with the sheep","to":"stayback"}]},"gift":{"text":"In a humble stable you find Mary and Joseph, and the Baby lying in a manger, just as the angel said. You kneel and gently place the little lamb nearby. The Saviour of the world has come, and He welcomed poor shepherds first.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"room","props":[["manger",50,88,1.3],["light",50,70,1.1],["sheep",72,88,0.7],["star",50,12,1]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"A gift for the King","lesson":"Jesus came for everyone: rich and poor, great and small. He welcomes you too.","verse":"For unto you is born this day in the city of David a Saviour, which is Christ the Lord.","ref":"Luke 2:11"}},"run":{"text":"You run through the quiet streets and see a soft light shining from a stable. There they are: Mary, Joseph, and the Baby in the manger! Afterwards you tell everyone you meet what the angels said, and all who hear it wonder.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"street","props":[["star",50,15,1.4],["town",50,84,1],["child",40,92,1,"#a1887f"],["person",60,92,0.9,"#5c6bc0"]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"Good news to share","lesson":"Good news is for sharing! We can tell others about Jesus with joy.","verse":"Fear not: for, behold, I bring you good tidings of great joy, which shall be to all people.","ref":"Luke 2:10"}},"stayback":{"text":"“Someone has to mind the sheep,” you say. The others' lanterns disappear down the hill towards Bethlehem. The fire burns low, and you doze off. When you wake, the gate of the fold is open and half the flock has wandered off into the dark hills. Somewhere far away, a lamb is crying.","art":{"sky":"dawn","ground":"hills","props":[["fire",45,90,0.8],["child",55,90,1,"#a1887f"],["person",78,90,0.9,"#6d4c41"],["person",88,90,0.9,"#8d6e63"]]},"sfx":"tension","choices":[{"text":"Pray, and wait for the dawn","to":"stayback_fix"},{"text":"Run off into the dark hills alone","to":"stayback_worse"}]},"stayback_fix":{"text":"You kneel by the embers and pray. At first light the lost sheep come wandering back, one by one. Then the shepherds return, their faces shining: they have seen the Saviour! Your father hugs you. The flock is safe, but you know you missed the greatest night the world has ever seen.","art":{"sky":"dawn","ground":"hills","props":[["fire",45,90,0.8],["child",55,90,1,"#a1887f"],["person",78,90,0.9,"#6d4c41"],["person",88,90,0.9,"#8d6e63"]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"Waiting for the dawn","lesson":"Staying behind cost you the blessing of seeing Jesus, but prayer brought help. Next time God calls, go!","verse":"I will lift up mine eyes unto the hills, from whence cometh my help.","ref":"Psalm 121:1"}},"stayback_worse":{"text":"You grab a burning stick and run into the hills. The wind blows it out. You trip over a rock, twist your ankle and lose your staff. You spend the rest of the night huddled behind a boulder, cold and afraid. At sunrise your father finds you limping, with only a few sheep nearby. On the way down, the other shepherds are singing: they saw the Saviour in Bethlehem. You saw nothing but the dark.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"hills","props":[["fire",45,90,0.8],["moon",82,16,1],["child",55,90,1,"#a1887f"]]},"sfx":"wind","end":{"type":"missed","title":"Lost in the dark hills","lesson":"You stayed behind when God called, then went your own way in the dark. The night you could have spent with the newborn King became the worst night of your life. When God calls, it is safest, and best, to go with Him.","verse":"To day if ye will hear his voice, harden not your heart.","ref":"Psalm 95:7-8"}}}},{"id":"boy-with-loaves","category":"bible","icon":"🍞","title":"The Boy with the Loaves","summary":"Your mother packed you a small lunch. Today it will feed thousands.","passage":{"label":"John 6","book":"John","chapter":6,"verse":1},"scenes":{"start":{"text":"You live by the Sea of Galilee. This morning your mother packed you a lunch: five little barley loaves and two small fish. “Don't lose it!” she smiles. Crowds of people are walking up the hillside. Everyone says Jesus is there, teaching and healing the sick.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"hills","props":[["basket",30,90,1],["child",40,90,1,"#ef8a3a"],["crowd",70,80,1],["sea",0,0,0]]},"choices":[{"text":"Sit near the front","to":"front"},{"text":"Climb a rock to see","to":"rock"}]},"front":{"text":"You squeeze through and sit on the soft grass near the front. Jesus is teaching about God's love. You watch a man who could not walk stand up and laugh with joy. You forget all about the time.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"hills","props":[["light",55,55,1],["crowd",30,86,0.9],["child",45,90,0.9,"#ef8a3a"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Keep listening","to":"hungry"}]},"rock":{"text":"You climb a big rock. From up here you can see thousands and thousands of people covering the hillside, more people than live in your whole town! Far away, near the lake, a gentle light seems to shine where Jesus is.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"hills","props":[["rocks",30,90,1.4],["child",30,74,1,"#ef8a3a"],["crowd",65,84,1.2],["crowd",85,86,0.8]]},"choices":[{"text":"Keep watching","to":"hungry"}]},"hungry":{"text":"The sun is going down and everyone is hungry. Jesus asks where they could buy bread. Philip says, “Even two hundred pennies' worth wouldn't be enough!” Andrew is walking through the crowd, looking for food. Your lunch is still in your basket.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"hills","props":[["crowd",40,86,1],["person",68,90,1,"#5c6bc0"],["child",78,90,0.9,"#ef8a3a"],["basket",85,92,0.7]]},"choices":[{"text":"Keep your lunch for yourself","to":"keep"},{"text":"Offer your lunch to Andrew","to":"offer"}]},"keep":{"text":"You hold your basket tightly. It's only a little lunch anyway, what good would it do for so many people? But you remember your mother's words: “Whatever we have comes from God, and we share it.”","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"hills","props":[["child",50,90,1.2,"#ef8a3a"],["basket",58,92,0.8]]},"choices":[{"text":"Offer it after all","to":"offer"},{"text":"Keep holding on to it","to":"keptlunch"}]},"offer":{"text":"You hold up your basket. Andrew brings you to Jesus and says, “There is a lad here, which hath five barley loaves, and two small fishes: but what are they among so many?” Jesus looks at you kindly. He takes your loaves, lifts His eyes to heaven and gives thanks.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"hills","props":[["light",45,55,1.2],["child",60,90,1,"#ef8a3a"],["basket",66,92,0.8],["person",30,90,1,"#5c6bc0"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Watch closely","to":"watch"}]},"watch":{"text":"The disciples begin handing out bread and fish, and it never runs out! Basket after basket, family after family. Five thousand men, plus women and children, all eat until they are full. You can hardly believe your eyes.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"hills","props":[["crowd",30,86,1],["crowd",70,86,1],["basket",50,92,1],["fish",58,90,0.8],["bread",42,90,0.8]]},"choices":[{"text":"Help gather the leftovers","to":"gather"},{"text":"Run home to tell your mother","to":"mother"}]},"gather":{"text":"Jesus says, “Gather up the fragments that remain, that nothing be lost.” You help the disciples collect the leftovers: twelve whole baskets full! Your little lunch, in Jesus' hands, fed thousands, with more to spare.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"hills","props":[["basket",30,92,0.9],["basket",45,92,0.9],["basket",60,92,0.9],["basket",75,92,0.9],["child",50,86,0.9,"#ef8a3a"]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"Twelve baskets full","lesson":"When we give Jesus the little we have, He can do great things with it.","verse":"I am the bread of life.","ref":"John 6:35"}},"mother":{"text":"You run all the way home. “Mother! Your five loaves fed five thousand people!” She laughs and hugs you, then listens with wide eyes to the whole story. That evening your family thanks God for His wonderful goodness.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"street","props":[["house",45,86,1.2],["child",62,92,1,"#ef8a3a"],["person",72,92,1,"#c2185b"]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"A small gift, a great miracle","lesson":"No gift is too small for God. Sharing what we have lets God work wonders.","verse":"Gather up the fragments that remain, that nothing be lost.","ref":"John 6:12"}},"keptlunch":{"text":"You hide your basket behind a rock and eat alone. Andrew finds another boy with five loaves, and Jesus feeds the whole crowd with them. Everyone is laughing and sharing. Then a woman points at your rock: “Look, that one hid his food while everyone was hungry!” Heads turn towards you.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"hills","props":[["rocks",25,90,1.2],["child",30,90,0.8,"#ef8a3a"],["crowd",65,86,1],["basket",75,92,0.8]]},"sfx":"crowd","choices":[{"text":"Say sorry and help gather the leftovers","to":"keptlunch_fix"},{"text":"Run off and hide","to":"keptlunch_worse"}]},"keptlunch_fix":{"text":"Your cheeks burn, but you walk over and help the disciples gather the leftovers: twelve baskets full. Andrew smiles at you. “It's not too late to help.” You didn't give your lunch, but now you know what giving can do.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"hills","props":[["rocks",25,90,1.2],["child",30,90,0.8,"#ef8a3a"],["crowd",65,86,1],["basket",75,92,0.8]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"Better late than never","lesson":"Selfishness made you miss the miracle, but joining in the work of love brought you back. Next time, give first.","verse":"Give, and it shall be given unto you.","ref":"Luke 6:38"}},"keptlunch_worse":{"text":"You run down the hillside and hide among the rocks until the crowd has gone. By then it's dark, and you don't know the way home. You wander for hours, hungry again, until your father finds you with a lantern, frantic with worry. Your mother has been crying. And the whole village is talking about the miracle you missed, and the boy who hid his bread.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"hills","props":[["rocks",25,90,1.2],["basket",75,92,0.8],["moon",82,16,1],["child",30,90,0.8,"#ef8a3a"]]},"sfx":"wind","end":{"type":"missed","title":"Alone in the dark","lesson":"Holding on to what we have made you miss a miracle and hurt the people who love you. What we give away blesses many; what we hide only leaves us alone.","verse":"There is that scattereth, and yet increaseth; and there is that withholdeth more than is meet, but it tendeth to poverty.","ref":"Proverbs 11:24"}}}},{"id":"other-little-boat","category":"bible","icon":"⛵","title":"The Other Little Boat","summary":"Jesus is crossing the lake, and your boat follows behind His. Then the storm comes.","passage":{"label":"Mark 4","book":"Mark","chapter":4,"verse":35},"scenes":{"start":{"text":"You are a fisherman's child in Capernaum. One evening Jesus says to His disciples, “Let us pass over unto the other side.” Their boat pushes off, and the Bible says there were also other little boats with them. You are in one of them, with your uncle.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"sea","props":[["boat",45,74,1.1],["boat",72,78,0.8],["child",72,70,0.5,"#26a69a"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Row close behind Jesus' boat","to":"close"},{"text":"Stay near the lanterns on the shore","to":"shore"}]},"close":{"text":"You row close behind. In the back of Jesus' boat you can see Him, fast asleep on a pillow, after a long day of teaching. The water is calm and the first stars appear.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"sea","props":[["boat",40,74,1.2],["light",36,62,0.6],["boat",72,78,0.9]]},"choices":[{"text":"Keep rowing","to":"storm"}]},"shore":{"text":"You stay near the lanterns on the shore for a while. “Come on,” says your uncle, “we'll follow the Teacher.” You row out into the dark lake behind the others.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"shore","props":[["lamp",20,86,0.9],["boat",60,76,1]]},"choices":[{"text":"Keep rowing","to":"storm"},{"text":"Refuse to go out on the lake","to":"stayshore"}]},"storm":{"text":"Suddenly a great storm of wind arises. Huge waves crash over the sides of the boats, filling them with water. Your uncle shouts, “Hold on!” The boat tips and rocks. You have never been so frightened.","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"sea","props":[["lightning",70,10,1],["boat",45,72,1.1],["boat",75,76,0.8]]},"choices":[{"text":"Shout for help","to":"shout"},{"text":"Pray: “Lord, save us!”","to":"pray"}]},"shout":{"text":"You shout as loud as you can, but the wind swallows your voice. Through the rain you see the disciples in the other boat, shaking Jesus awake: “Master, carest thou not that we perish?”","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"sea","props":[["boat",40,72,1.2],["boat",75,76,0.9]]},"choices":[{"text":"Watch what Jesus does","to":"calm"}]},"pray":{"text":"You close your eyes and pray with all your heart: “Lord, save us!” When you open them, you see the disciples waking Jesus: “Master, carest thou not that we perish?”","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"sea","props":[["boat",40,72,1.2],["light",40,60,0.6],["boat",75,76,0.9]]},"choices":[{"text":"Watch what Jesus does","to":"calm"}]},"calm":{"text":"Jesus stands up. He speaks to the wind and says to the sea, “Peace, be still.” At once the wind stops. The waves lie down flat. There is a great calm. The disciples whisper to one another, “What manner of man is this, that even the wind and the sea obey him?”","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"sea","props":[["light",40,56,1.4],["boat",40,74,1.2],["boat",75,78,0.9],["moon",80,18,1]]},"choices":[{"text":"Ask your uncle who Jesus is","to":"ask"},{"text":"Sit quietly and thank God","to":"thank"}]},"ask":{"text":"“Uncle,” you whisper, “who is Jesus, that the sea obeys Him?” Your uncle is quiet for a long time. “The psalms say only God can calm the sea,” he says at last. “Child, I think we have seen something holy tonight.”","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"sea","props":[["boat",50,76,1.3],["moon",78,16,1]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"Lord of the wind and waves","lesson":"Jesus is Lord of all creation. Even the wind and the sea obey Him.","verse":"He maketh the storm a calm, so that the waves thereof are still.","ref":"Psalm 107:29"}},"thank":{"text":"You sit very still in the gently rocking boat and thank God. The stars shine above the quiet lake. You know you will never forget this night, and that you never need to be afraid alone, because Jesus is near.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"sea","props":[["boat",50,76,1.3],["moon",20,16,1]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"Peace in the storm","lesson":"When we are afraid, we can call on Jesus. He brings peace.","verse":"Peace, be still.","ref":"Mark 4:39"}},"stayshore":{"text":"“I don't want to go,” you say, and your uncle sails off without you. Your mother asks you to pull the family's little boat up the beach and bring in the nets before dark. But you're sulking, so you leave it for later. That night a terrible storm roars across the lake.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"shore","props":[["house",25,88,1],["child",45,92,0.9,"#26a69a"],["person",65,92,1,"#6d4c41"],["boat",82,78,0.7]]},"sfx":"thunder","choices":[{"text":"Wake your mother and tell her","to":"stayshore_fix"},{"text":"Run down to the beach alone","to":"stayshore_worse"}]},"stayshore_fix":{"text":"You wake your mother. Together, with a neighbour, you drag the boat up the beach just in time. In the morning the fishermen come back amazed: Jesus stood up in the storm, and it obeyed Him! You missed the wonder, but you learned to do your jobs when you're asked.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"shore","props":[["house",25,88,1],["child",45,92,0.9,"#26a69a"],["person",65,92,1,"#6d4c41"],["boat",82,78,0.7]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"Just in time","lesson":"Fear kept you on the shore, and sulking nearly cost your family their boat. Obeying, and asking for help, protects the people we love.","verse":"Children, obey your parents in the Lord: for this is right.","ref":"Ephesians 6:1"}},"stayshore_worse":{"text":"You run down to the beach alone. The wind is screaming. You grab the rope, but a wave rips it out of your hands, and the little boat is dragged out into the black water with all the nets. You stumble home soaked and shivering. In the morning the boat is gone, and with it your family's way of earning bread. The fishermen come back singing about the Teacher who calmed the sea. You weren't there.","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"shore","props":[["house",25,88,1],["boat",82,78,0.7],["child",45,92,0.9,"#26a69a"]]},"sfx":"thunder","end":{"type":"missed","title":"Lost to the storm","lesson":"You stayed away from Jesus, then ignored what you were asked to do, and your family lost their boat. Staying close to Jesus, and obeying, would have spared you both.","verse":"Then they cry unto the LORD in their trouble, and he bringeth them out of their distresses.","ref":"Psalm 107:28"}}}},{"id":"up-the-sycamore","category":"bible","icon":"🌳","title":"Up the Sycamore Tree","summary":"Jesus is coming through Jericho, but you're too small to see over the crowd.","passage":{"label":"Luke 19","book":"Luke","chapter":19,"verse":1},"scenes":{"start":{"text":"The streets of Jericho are packed with people. “Jesus is coming!” someone shouts. You stand on tiptoe, but all you can see are backs and elbows. You are much too small to see anything.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["crowd",50,86,1.3],["child",20,92,0.9,"#7e57c2"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Squeeze through the crowd","to":"squeeze"},{"text":"Look for a high place","to":"high"}]},"squeeze":{"text":"You wriggle between people's legs. Someone steps on your toe. Then you spot a short man in fine clothes hurrying along. People mutter, “That's Zacchaeus, the chief tax collector. He takes more money than he should!”","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["crowd",40,86,1],["person",68,92,0.8,"#1565c0"],["child",55,92,0.8,"#7e57c2"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Follow him","to":"tree"},{"text":"Stay where you are","to":"stay"}]},"high":{"text":"You look around for somewhere high. There's a big sycamore tree by the road! But someone is already scrambling up its branches: a short man in fine clothes. It's Zacchaeus, the tax collector nobody likes.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["sycamore",60,90,1.3],["person",60,50,0.6,"#1565c0"],["child",30,92,0.9,"#7e57c2"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Climb up on a low branch","to":"tree"}]},"stay":{"text":"You stay where you are and can't see a thing. Then, suddenly, the whole crowd goes quiet. You push forward to see why everyone is looking up into a sycamore tree.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["sycamore",65,90,1.2],["crowd",35,88,1]]},"choices":[{"text":"Look up","to":"tree"}]},"tree":{"text":"Jesus stops right under the tree. He looks up and says, “Zacchaeus, make haste, and come down; for to day I must abide at thy house.” Zacchaeus nearly falls out of the tree with joy! But people grumble, “He's going to eat with a sinner!”","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["sycamore",55,90,1.3],["light",40,70,0.8],["crowd",80,88,0.8]]},"choices":[{"text":"Grumble with the crowd","to":"grumble"},{"text":"Wonder why Jesus chose him","to":"wonder"}]},"grumble":{"text":"You frown and cross your arms like everyone else. But then you see Zacchaeus's face. He is smiling like someone who has just been given the greatest gift in the world. Your frown slowly fades.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["person",50,92,1,"#1565c0"],["crowd",80,88,0.8],["child",25,92,0.8,"#7e57c2"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Keep watching","to":"change"},{"text":"Walk away grumbling","to":"walkaway"}]},"wonder":{"text":"Why would Jesus choose Zacchaeus, of all people? Maybe Jesus sees something in him that nobody else can see. You follow along to find out.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["child",40,92,1,"#7e57c2"],["house",70,86,1]]},"choices":[{"text":"Keep watching","to":"change"}]},"change":{"text":"At his house, Zacchaeus stands up and says, “Lord, I will give half of everything I have to the poor. And if I have cheated anyone, I will pay back four times as much!” Jesus says, “This day is salvation come to this house.”","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"room","props":[["table",50,90,1.2],["light",40,65,0.8],["person",62,90,1,"#1565c0"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Go home and tell your family","to":"home"},{"text":"Decide to be kind to someone left out","to":"kind"}]},"home":{"text":"You run home and tell your family everything. “Jesus went to Zacchaeus's house! And now Zacchaeus is giving to the poor!” Your father smiles. “So Jesus came to find people who are lost, even the ones everyone else gives up on.”","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["house",40,86,1.1],["child",60,92,1,"#7e57c2"],["person",72,92,1,"#6d4c41"]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"Seeking the lost","lesson":"Jesus looks for everyone who is lost, and nobody is too far away for His love.","verse":"For the Son of man is come to seek and to save that which was lost.","ref":"Luke 19:10"}},"kind":{"text":"There's a boy in your street that nobody plays with. Tomorrow, you decide, you will say hello and ask him to play. If Jesus could see the good in Zacchaeus, you can try to see the good in others too.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["child",40,92,1,"#7e57c2"],["child",60,92,1,"#43a047"]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"Seeing with Jesus' eyes","lesson":"People look at the outside, but God looks at the heart. We can see others as Jesus does.","verse":"for man looketh on the outward appearance, but the LORD looketh on the heart.","ref":"1 Samuel 16:7"}},"walkaway":{"text":"“Why would Jesus visit a cheat?” you mutter, and you stomp off. At the well you tell everyone that Zacchaeus is fooling Jesus, and you add a few things that aren't quite true. People nod and whisper, and the story starts to spread.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["house",30,86,1.1],["child",50,92,0.9,"#7e57c2"],["crowd",78,88,0.8]]},"sfx":"crowd","choices":[{"text":"Go back and see what really happened","to":"walkaway_fix"},{"text":"Keep spreading the story","to":"walkaway_worse"}]},"walkaway_fix":{"text":"You run back to Zacchaeus's house and hear him promise to give half of everything to the poor. Your face goes hot. You hurry back to the well and tell everyone, “I was wrong. He's changed.” Some people frown at you, but the unkind story stops with you.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["house",30,86,1.1],["child",50,92,0.9,"#7e57c2"],["crowd",78,88,0.8]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"Taking it back","lesson":"Gossip spreads fast, but going back to tell the truth stops it. Jesus sees what others miss.","verse":"Judge not, that ye be not judged.","ref":"Matthew 7:1"}},"walkaway_worse":{"text":"By evening your story has spread through the whole town. Then the news arrives: Zacchaeus has given half of everything to the poor and paid back four times what he took, even to your own neighbour. Everyone knows the things you said weren't true. Your neighbour won't look at you, and your father makes you go door to door to say sorry. You missed the day salvation came to Jericho, and made yourself the one nobody trusts.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"street","props":[["house",30,86,1.1],["child",50,92,0.9,"#7e57c2"]]},"sfx":"sting","end":{"type":"missed","title":"The story that wasn't true","lesson":"Judging and gossip hurt Zacchaeus, and hurt you most of all. Jesus came to seek the lost; we should hope for people, not tear them down.","verse":"A froward man soweth strife: and a whisperer separateth chief friends.","ref":"Proverbs 16:28"}}}},{"id":"secret-gift","category":"saints","icon":"🎁","title":"The Secret Gift","summary":"A poor family next door is in trouble, and one night you see Bishop Nicholas walking by.","passage":{"label":"Matthew 6","book":"Matthew","chapter":6,"verse":1},"scenes":{"start":{"text":"You live in the town of Myra. Next door lives a poor father with three daughters. Tonight you hear them crying through the wall. They have no money for food, and no money for the girls' weddings. Their father is in despair.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"street","props":[["house",35,86,1.2],["window",35,70,1],["house",70,86,1],["moon",82,16,1]]},"choices":[{"text":"Tell your parents","to":"parents"},{"text":"Pray for the family","to":"pray"}]},"parents":{"text":"You tell your mother. She sighs sadly. “We have very little ourselves, but we will pray for them, and share some bread tomorrow.” You lie awake, wishing you could do more.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"room","props":[["lamp",30,80,1],["child",55,90,1,"#26a69a"],["person",70,90,1,"#c2185b"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Look out of the window","to":"nicholas"}]},"pray":{"text":"You kneel by your bed in front of the little icon lamp and pray, “Lord, please help our neighbours.” Then you hear soft footsteps outside.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"room","props":[["icon",40,62,1],["lamp",40,78,0.8],["child",55,90,1,"#26a69a"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Look out of the window","to":"nicholas"}]},"nicholas":{"text":"In the moonlight you see a man walking quietly down the street, carrying a heavy bag. It's the good bishop, Nicholas! He looks around carefully, as if he doesn't want anyone to see him.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"street","props":[["person",55,92,1.1,"#b71c1c","halo"],["gold",62,92,0.7],["house",25,86,1],["moon",80,16,1]]},"choices":[{"text":"Call out his name","to":"call"},{"text":"Watch silently","to":"watch"}]},"call":{"text":"“Bishop Nicholas!” you whisper loudly. He turns, smiles, and puts a finger to his lips. “Shh,” he says softly. “This is a secret between God and them. Can you keep a secret?” You nod.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"street","props":[["person",55,92,1.1,"#b71c1c","halo"],["window",25,62,1],["house",25,86,1]]},"choices":[{"text":"Keep watching","to":"drop"}]},"watch":{"text":"You hold your breath and watch. Nicholas reaches the neighbours' window, and with a quick throw, tosses the bag inside. Then he slips away into the dark, as quietly as he came.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"street","props":[["house",40,86,1.2],["window",40,70,1],["person",70,92,1,"#b71c1c","halo"],["moon",85,16,1]]},"choices":[{"text":"Listen","to":"drop"}]},"drop":{"text":"Clink! You hear a bag of gold land on the floor next door. Then you hear gasps, then laughing, then crying for joy! In the morning the whole street is talking: “Who gave them the gold?” Everyone looks at you, because your window faces theirs.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["house",40,86,1.1],["person",60,92,1,"#6d4c41"],["child",72,92,0.9,"#26a69a"],["gold",30,92,0.7]]},"choices":[{"text":"Tell everyone it was Nicholas","to":"tell"},{"text":"Keep his secret","to":"keep"}]},"tell":{"text":"“It was Bishop Nicholas!” you announce. Soon crowds gather at the church to praise him. But when you see Nicholas, he looks sad. “I wanted them to thank God, not me,” he says gently. “When we give, we give for God to see.”","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["church",60,86,1],["crowd",35,88,0.9],["child",78,92,0.8,"#26a69a"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Say sorry and promise to keep secrets","to":"tellsorry"},{"text":"Keep telling everyone that you knew first","to":"brag"}]},"keep":{"text":"You say nothing. Twice more the gold arrives by night, one bag for each daughter. The third time, the father hides and catches Nicholas! He falls at his feet to thank him. Nicholas lifts him up and asks him to tell no one, and to thank God alone.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"street","props":[["person",45,92,1.1,"#b71c1c","halo"],["person",62,92,1,"#6d4c41"],["gold",53,94,0.6],["moon",82,16,1]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"A secret kept for God","lesson":"Like Saint Nicholas, we can help others quietly, out of love. God sees what is done in secret. The Church remembers him every year on 6 December.","verse":"and thy Father which seeth in secret himself shall reward thee openly.","ref":"Matthew 6:4"}},"tellsorry":{"text":"“I'm sorry, Father Nicholas,” you say. He smiles and blesses you. “Now you know the secret of secret gifts. God sees them, and that is enough.” From that day on, you help people quietly too.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["person",45,92,1.1,"#b71c1c","halo"],["child",60,92,0.9,"#26a69a"],["church",82,86,0.8]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"The gift that wanted to stay secret","lesson":"Jesus teaches us to give quietly, not to be praised, but out of love, for God to see.","verse":"But when thou doest alms, let not thy left hand know what thy right hand doeth.","ref":"Matthew 6:3"}},"brag":{"text":"You tell the whole market that you saw the bishop first. By noon, a crowd has gathered outside the poor family's house, staring and gossiping. The three girls hide inside, ashamed.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["house",40,86,1.1],["crowd",68,88,1],["child",25,92,0.9,"#26a69a"]]},"sfx":"crowd","choices":[{"text":"Tell the crowd to leave them in peace","to":"brag_fix"},{"text":"Tell them even more","to":"brag_worse"}]},"brag_fix":{"text":"“Please, leave them alone,” you say, and slowly the crowd drifts away. You knock on the door and say sorry. The eldest daughter forgives you. That night, when Nicholas passes again, you keep his secret.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["house",40,86,1.1],["crowd",68,88,1],["child",25,92,0.9,"#26a69a"]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"Mending the damage","lesson":"Gossip spilled a kind secret and hurt people. Asking forgiveness, and protecting them, began to put it right.","verse":"A talebearer revealeth secrets: but he that is of a faithful spirit concealeth the matter.","ref":"Proverbs 11:13"}},"brag_worse":{"text":"You tell them everything: the bag, the window, even what you heard through the wall. The gossip grows, and people say cruel things about the family. A few weeks later they pack their cart and move to another town where nobody knows them. The youngest daughter, your friend, doesn't wave goodbye. And Nicholas never walks down your street at night again.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"street","props":[["house",40,86,1.1],["child",25,92,0.9,"#26a69a"]]},"sfx":"sting","end":{"type":"missed","title":"A secret spilled","lesson":"Gossip turned a kind gift into shame and drove a family away. Some words can't be taken back; keeping good secrets is part of love.","verse":"The words of a talebearer are as wounds.","ref":"Proverbs 18:8"}}}},{"id":"shipwreck-paul","category":"saints","icon":"⚓","title":"Shipwreck with Saint Paul","summary":"You are the cook's helper on a great ship, and one of the passengers is a prisoner named Paul.","passage":{"label":"Acts 27","book":"Acts","chapter":27,"verse":1},"scenes":{"start":{"text":"You are the cook's helper on a big grain ship sailing to Rome. Among the passengers is a prisoner named Paul, guarded by a kind centurion named Julius. At a harbour called Fair Havens, Paul warns everyone, “Sirs, this voyage will be dangerous. We may lose the ship!” But the captain wants to sail on.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"shore","props":[["ship",55,78,1.2],["person",25,92,1,"#795548","halo"],["child",35,92,0.8,"#ef6c00"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Tell the cook you agree with Paul","to":"agree"},{"text":"Get on with your work","to":"busy"}]},"agree":{"text":"“I think Paul is right,” you tell the cook. He shrugs. “The captain decides, not us.” The centurion listens to the captain, and the ship sails out with a gentle south wind.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"sea","props":[["ship",50,76,1.2]]},"choices":[{"text":"Sail on","to":"storm"}]},"busy":{"text":"You get on with peeling vegetables. The captain and the owner decide to sail. At first a gentle south wind blows, and everyone thinks Paul was wrong.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"sea","props":[["ship",50,76,1.2],["sun2",80,20,1]]},"choices":[{"text":"Sail on","to":"storm"}]},"storm":{"text":"Then a fierce wind called Euroclydon roars down from the mountains. The ship is caught and driven wildly across the sea. For many days there is neither sun nor stars, only wind, rain and giant waves. Everyone loses hope of being saved.","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"sea","props":[["lightning",25,10,1],["ship",50,74,1.2]]},"choices":[{"text":"Hide below deck","to":"hide"},{"text":"Stay near Paul","to":"near"}]},"hide":{"text":"You hide below deck among the sacks of grain, trembling every time the ship crashes into a wave. Then you hear a calm voice up above. It's Paul, speaking to everyone.","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"sea","props":[["ship",50,74,1.2]]},"choices":[{"text":"Go up and listen","to":"speaks"}]},"near":{"text":"You stay close to Paul. Even in the storm, he prays quietly. There is something peaceful about him, as if he knows a secret. Then he stands up to speak to everyone.","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"sea","props":[["ship",50,74,1.2],["light",42,58,0.5]]},"choices":[{"text":"Listen","to":"speaks"}]},"speaks":{"text":"Paul says, “Be of good cheer: for there shall be no loss of any man's life among you, but of the ship. For there stood by me this night the angel of God, whose I am, and whom I serve. I believe God, that it shall be even as it was told me.”","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"sea","props":[["angel",70,35,1],["ship",45,74,1.2]]},"choices":[{"text":"Believe Paul","to":"believe"},{"text":"Worry anyway","to":"worry"}]},"worry":{"text":"You still feel scared. Paul notices your face and kneels beside you. “I know it's hard,” he says. “But I believe God. He has never let me down. Let's trust Him together.” You feel a little braver.","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"sea","props":[["person",45,92,1,"#795548","halo"],["child",56,92,0.8,"#ef6c00"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Stay close to Paul","to":"bread"},{"text":"Refuse to listen and hide","to":"nopeace"}]},"believe":{"text":"You decide to believe Paul. A strange peace fills your heart, even though the storm still roars. God has promised that everyone will live!","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"sea","props":[["ship",50,74,1.2],["light",50,50,0.6]]},"choices":[{"text":"Wait with the others","to":"bread"}]},"bread":{"text":"On the fourteenth night, Paul urges everyone to eat. He takes bread, gives thanks to God in front of them all, breaks it and begins to eat. Everyone is cheered up and eats too. All together there are 276 people on the ship.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"room","props":[["table",50,90,1.2],["bread",50,78,1],["lamp",30,80,0.8],["person",68,90,1,"#795548","halo"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Hold on through the night","to":"ground"}]},"ground":{"text":"At dawn they see a beach. The ship runs aground and begins to break apart in the waves! The centurion orders those who can swim to jump first, and the rest to follow on boards and pieces of the ship.","art":{"sky":"dawn","ground":"shore","props":[["ship",55,76,1.1,"broken"],["child",30,86,0.7,"#ef6c00"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Swim for the shore","to":"malta"},{"text":"Hold on to a board","to":"malta"}]},"malta":{"text":"Every single person reaches the land safely, just as God promised! The island is called Malta. The islanders are very kind and light a fire in the rain to warm everyone. A viper leaps out of the sticks and bites Paul's hand, but he shakes it into the fire and is not harmed at all.","art":{"sky":"dawn","ground":"shore","props":[["fire",45,90,1.3],["person",58,92,1,"#795548","halo"],["child",32,92,0.8,"#ef6c00"],["person",72,92,1,"#5d4037"]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"Everyone saved","lesson":"Saint Paul trusted God in the storm, and God kept His promise. We can trust God in our own storms too.","verse":"Wherefore, sirs, be of good cheer: for I believe God, that it shall be even as it was told me.","ref":"Acts 27:25"}},"nopeace":{"text":"You cover your ears and hide deep among the sacks for days. On the fourteenth night, when Paul gives thanks and everyone eats, you stay hidden and hungry. At dawn, the ship strikes the sandbank with a terrible crack.","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"sea","props":[["ship",50,74,1.2,"broken"],["child",25,90,0.6,"#ef6c00"]]},"sfx":"crash","choices":[{"text":"Climb up and find Paul","to":"nopeace_fix"},{"text":"Stay hidden below","to":"nopeace_worse"}]},"nopeace_fix":{"text":"You scramble up the ladder. Paul grabs your hand: “Hold this board and kick!” You reach the beach with the others, exhausted but safe, just as God promised.","art":{"sky":"dawn","ground":"sea","props":[["ship",50,74,1.2,"broken"],["child",25,90,0.6,"#ef6c00"]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"Trusting at the last","lesson":"Fear made you hide from God's promise and go hungry, but coming out and trusting at last brought you safely to shore.","verse":"Be careful for nothing; but in every thing by prayer and supplication with thanksgiving let your requests be made known unto God.","ref":"Philippians 4:6"}},"nopeace_worse":{"text":"Water pours into the hold. You're trapped among floating sacks and can't find the ladder. You shout until your voice is gone. At last two sailors hear you and pull you out, and you're dragged onto the beach last of all, freezing, with everything you owned lost to the sea. God kept His promise: everyone was saved. But while the others had peace, you had only terror, and now you have nothing but wet clothes.","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"sea","props":[["ship",50,74,1.2,"broken"],["child",25,90,0.6,"#ef6c00"]]},"sfx":"waves","end":{"type":"missed","title":"Trapped in the hold","lesson":"God's promise was for everyone, but you refused to listen and hid from it. Those who trusted Him had peace and courage; you had fear and loss.","verse":"Thou wilt keep him in perfect peace, whose mind is stayed on thee: because he trusteth in thee.","ref":"Isaiah 26:3"}}}},{"id":"shepherd-bishop","category":"saints","icon":"🐑","title":"The Shepherd Bishop","summary":"You help Saint Spyridon look after his sheep. One night, thieves come.","passage":{"label":"Luke 6","book":"Luke","chapter":6,"verse":27},"scenes":{"start":{"text":"On the island of Cyprus lives a bishop named Spyridon. Even though he is a bishop, he still looks after his own sheep, and you help him. As the sun sets, you lead the flock into the sheepfold.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"hills","props":[["sheep",20,88,0.9],["sheep",32,90,0.9],["person",55,92,1,"#795548","halo"],["child",68,92,0.8,"#43a047"],["fence",85,90,1]]},"choices":[{"text":"Count the sheep","to":"count"},{"text":"Ask why a bishop keeps sheep","to":"ask"}]},"count":{"text":"You count carefully: every sheep is there. You close the gate of the fold, and Spyridon blesses you. “Good night, little shepherd,” he says.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"hills","props":[["fence",50,90,1.3],["sheep",40,86,0.8],["sheep",55,86,0.8],["child",75,92,0.8,"#43a047"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Go to sleep","to":"night"}]},"ask":{"text":"“Why does a bishop look after sheep?” you ask. Spyridon smiles. “Our Lord Jesus is the Good Shepherd. A bishop is a shepherd of people. And there is nothing shameful about humble work. God loves a humble heart.”","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"hills","props":[["person",45,92,1.1,"#795548","halo"],["child",60,92,0.8,"#43a047"],["sheep",80,88,0.8]]},"choices":[{"text":"Go to sleep","to":"night"}]},"night":{"text":"In the middle of the night you wake up. There are noises by the sheepfold: some thieves are climbing over the fence to steal the sheep!","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"hills","props":[["fence",50,90,1.3],["person",40,90,0.9,"#37474f"],["person",60,90,0.9,"#263238"],["moon",82,16,1]]},"choices":[{"text":"Run to wake Spyridon","to":"wake"},{"text":"Pray quietly","to":"pray"}]},"wake":{"text":"You run to wake Spyridon. But he only smiles and says, “Don't be afraid. God is watching over the sheep. Go back to sleep, and we will see in the morning.”","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"room","props":[["lamp",35,80,0.9],["person",55,90,1,"#795548","halo"],["child",70,90,0.8,"#43a047"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Wait for morning","to":"stuck"}]},"pray":{"text":"You whisper, “Lord, protect our sheep.” Somehow you feel peaceful, and you fall asleep again.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"room","props":[["icon",40,62,1],["lamp",40,78,0.8],["child",55,90,1,"#43a047"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Wait for morning","to":"stuck"}]},"stuck":{"text":"In the morning you find something amazing: the thieves are standing in the sheepfold, unable to move, as if invisible hands were holding them there all night! The Church remembers this wonder in Saint Spyridon's life. They look tired and frightened.","art":{"sky":"dawn","ground":"hills","props":[["fence",50,90,1.3],["person",42,90,0.9,"#37474f"],["person",58,90,0.9,"#263238"],["light",50,40,0.8]]},"choices":[{"text":"Ask Spyridon to punish them","to":"punish"},{"text":"Wait and see what he does","to":"wait"}]},"punish":{"text":"“They should be punished!” you say. Spyridon puts his hand on your shoulder. “Our Lord taught us to be merciful, as our Father in heaven is merciful,” he says gently. “Watch.”","art":{"sky":"dawn","ground":"hills","props":[["person",45,92,1.1,"#795548","halo"],["child",60,92,0.8,"#43a047"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Watch","to":"mercy"},{"text":"Throw a stone at the thieves","to":"stones"}]},"wait":{"text":"You wait quietly to see what the holy bishop will do.","art":{"sky":"dawn","ground":"hills","props":[["person",45,92,1.1,"#795548","halo"],["child",60,92,0.8,"#43a047"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Watch","to":"mercy"}]},"mercy":{"text":"Spyridon prays, and the thieves can move again. He tells them kindly to work honestly from now on. Then he gives them a ram from the flock and says, “Take this, so your sleepless night is not wasted.” The thieves are so moved that they say sorry and go away changed.","art":{"sky":"dawn","ground":"hills","props":[["person",40,92,1.1,"#795548","halo"],["sheep",52,90,0.8],["person",66,92,0.9,"#37474f"],["child",80,92,0.7,"#43a047"]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"Mercy wins hearts","lesson":"Saint Spyridon showed mercy instead of punishment, and mercy changed the thieves' hearts.","verse":"Be ye therefore merciful, as your Father also is merciful.","ref":"Luke 6:36"}},"stones":{"text":"You throw a stone. It misses the thieves and cracks against the fence, and the frightened sheep burst out of the fold and scatter across the hills. Spyridon looks at you with great sadness.","art":{"sky":"dawn","ground":"hills","props":[["person",40,92,1.1,"#795548","halo"],["child",55,92,0.8,"#43a047"],["rocks",62,92,0.4],["person",80,92,0.9,"#37474f"]]},"sfx":"sheep","choices":[{"text":"Ask Spyridon to forgive you and help gather the sheep","to":"stones_fix"},{"text":"Say it's the thieves' fault","to":"stones_worse"}]},"stones_fix":{"text":"“Forgive me,” you whisper. Spyridon forgives you, then shows mercy to the thieves too, and they even help to round up the sheep. By evening every sheep is home.","art":{"sky":"dawn","ground":"hills","props":[["person",40,92,1.1,"#795548","halo"],["child",55,92,0.8,"#43a047"],["rocks",62,92,0.4],["person",80,92,0.9,"#37474f"]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"Mercy for me too","lesson":"Anger scattered the flock, but asking forgiveness brought peace. Spyridon forgave you just as he forgave the thieves.","verse":"Be ye therefore merciful, as your Father also is merciful.","ref":"Luke 6:36"}},"stones_worse":{"text":"“It's their fault!” you shout. You spend the whole day alone chasing sheep over the rocky hills, sunburnt and scratched. Three lambs are never found. That evening you hear that the thieves said sorry and went away changed by Spyridon's kindness. But they flinch whenever they see you.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"hills","props":[["rocks",62,92,0.4],["child",55,92,0.8,"#43a047"]]},"sfx":"wind","end":{"type":"missed","title":"A stone thrown in anger","lesson":"Anger wanted revenge, refused to take the blame, and lost three lambs. Mercy changes hearts; revenge only scatters.","verse":"Be not overcome of evil, but overcome evil with good.","ref":"Romans 12:21"}}}},{"id":"lost-wallet","category":"life","icon":"👛","title":"The Lost Wallet","summary":"On the way home from school, you find a wallet full of money.","passage":{"label":"Luke 16","book":"Luke","chapter":16,"verse":10},"scenes":{"start":{"text":"On your way home from school, you spot something on the pavement: a brown wallet. Inside there is money, quite a lot of money, and a card with a name on it.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["wallet",45,92,1],["child",60,92,1,"#1e88e5"],["house",25,86,1]]},"choices":[{"text":"Keep the money","to":"keep"},{"text":"Look for the owner's name","to":"look"},{"text":"Give it to a grown-up","to":"grownup"}]},"keep":{"text":"You imagine all the sweets and toys you could buy. But as you walk, the wallet feels heavier and heavier in your pocket. Someone out there has lost this. Maybe they need it.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["child",50,92,1,"#1e88e5"],["wallet",58,90,0.6]]},"choices":[{"text":"Change your mind","to":"look"},{"text":"Keep it anyway","to":"keepend"}]},"keepend":{"text":"You buy sweets with some of the money. But they don't taste sweet at all. At home you can't stop thinking about the person who lost it.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"room","props":[["child",45,90,1,"#1e88e5"],["person",60,90,1,"#c2185b"],["wallet",52,82,0.6]]},"choices":[{"text":"Tell your mother everything","to":"keeptell"},{"text":"Hide the wallet and say nothing","to":"hidewallet"}]},"look":{"text":"You look at the card inside. It belongs to Mrs Anna Petrou, and her address is just two streets away.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["child",45,92,1,"#1e88e5"],["wallet",53,86,0.6],["house",75,86,1]]},"choices":[{"text":"Take it to her with a grown-up","to":"return"},{"text":"Post it through her door","to":"post"}]},"grownup":{"text":"You give the wallet to your father as soon as you get home. “Well done,” he says. He finds the owner's name inside: Mrs Anna Petrou, who lives nearby. “Let's take it to her together.”","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"room","props":[["child",45,90,1,"#1e88e5"],["person",60,90,1.1,"#5d4037"],["wallet",52,82,0.6]]},"choices":[{"text":"Go together","to":"return"}]},"post":{"text":"You are about to push it through her letterbox, when you remember that your parents always say not to go to strangers' houses alone, and that money could get lost. You run home to ask your mother to come with you.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["house",55,86,1.2],["child",35,92,0.9,"#1e88e5"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Go back with your mother","to":"return"}]},"return":{"text":"An elderly lady opens the door. When she sees the wallet her eyes fill with tears. “Oh, thank you! That was the money for my medicine this month!” She offers you some money as a reward.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["house",55,86,1.2],["person",62,92,1,"#8e24aa"],["child",45,92,0.9,"#1e88e5"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Accept the reward","to":"accept"},{"text":"Say, “No thank you, I'm glad to help”","to":"refuse"}]},"accept":{"text":"You thank her politely. On the way home you decide to put some of the reward in the church box for people in need. Your heart feels light and happy.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["church",65,86,1],["child",40,92,1,"#1e88e5"]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"An honest heart","lesson":"Honesty brings joy, to others and to us. It's fine to accept a thank-you gift, and even better to share it.","verse":"He that is faithful in that which is least is faithful also in much.","ref":"Luke 16:10"}},"refuse":{"text":"“No thank you, I'm just glad to help,” you say. Mrs Petrou hugs you. “God bless you, child. You have made an old lady very happy today.”","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["house",55,86,1.2],["person",62,92,1,"#8e24aa"],["child",50,92,0.9,"#1e88e5"],["light",56,55,0.5]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"A light for others","lesson":"When we do good, people see God's love shining through us.","verse":"Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven.","ref":"Matthew 5:16"}},"keeptell":{"text":"At last you tell your mother everything. She is sad, but she helps you find the owner and give the wallet back, and you use your own savings to replace what you spent. It's hard, but your heart feels clean again.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"room","props":[["child",45,90,1,"#1e88e5"],["person",60,90,1,"#c2185b"],["wallet",52,82,0.6]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"It's never too late to put things right","lesson":"Keeping what isn't ours makes our heart heavy. Being honest in small things matters to God, and it's always good to put things right.","verse":"He that is faithful in that which is least is faithful also in much.","ref":"Luke 16:10"}},"hidewallet":{"text":"You push the wallet to the back of a drawer. A week later you hear that old Mrs Petrou from two streets away couldn't buy her medicine this month, because she lost her wallet. Your stomach twists.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"room","props":[["child",50,90,1,"#1e88e5"],["wallet",60,86,0.6]]},"sfx":"tension","choices":[{"text":"Take it back to her straight away","to":"hidewallet_fix"},{"text":"Leave it in the drawer","to":"hidewallet_worse"}]},"hidewallet_fix":{"text":"You run to her house with your mother, give the wallet back, and confess that you spent some of the money. Mrs Petrou is quiet for a moment, then forgives you. Over the next weeks, you pay back every coin from your pocket money.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"room","props":[["child",50,90,1,"#1e88e5"],["wallet",60,86,0.6]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"Never too late","lesson":"Hiding the wallet hurt someone in need, but it's never too late to return what isn't ours and make things right.","verse":"He that covereth his sins shall not prosper: but whoso confesseth and forsaketh them shall have mercy.","ref":"Proverbs 28:13"}},"hidewallet_worse":{"text":"You leave it there. A few days later an ambulance stops outside Mrs Petrou's house: without her medicine she became ill and has to stay in hospital for a while. The doctors say she will get better. Then your mother finds the wallet while tidying your drawer, and her face goes pale. You have to go to the hospital, give it back, and tell Mrs Petrou what you did. It's the hardest thing you have ever done.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"room","props":[["wallet",60,86,0.6],["moon",82,16,1],["child",50,90,1,"#1e88e5"]]},"sfx":"sting","end":{"type":"missed","title":"The wallet in the drawer","lesson":"Keeping what wasn't yours made someone ill and broke your family's trust. Small dishonest choices can grow into great harm.","verse":"He that walketh uprightly walketh surely: but he that perverteth his ways shall be known.","ref":"Proverbs 10:9"}}}},{"id":"new-girl","category":"life","icon":"🤗","title":"The New Girl","summary":"There's a new girl in your class, and she's sitting alone at lunch.","passage":{"label":"Luke 6","book":"Luke","chapter":6,"verse":31},"scenes":{"start":{"text":"A new girl named Mariam has joined your class. She comes from far away and speaks with a different accent. At lunchtime she sits all alone. Some children whisper and giggle about her.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"grass","props":[["school",25,84,1],["bench",60,92,1],["child",60,86,0.8,"#ec407a"],["child",82,92,0.8,"#1e88e5"],["child",90,92,0.8,"#43a047"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Go and sit with her","to":"sit"},{"text":"Stay with your friends","to":"friends"}]},"friends":{"text":"You stay with your friends. One of them copies Mariam's accent, and everyone laughs. “Go on, you say something too!” they tell you.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"grass","props":[["child",40,92,0.9,"#1e88e5"],["child",52,92,0.9,"#43a047"],["child",64,92,0.9,"#fb8c00"],["bench",88,92,0.7]]},"choices":[{"text":"Laugh along","to":"laugh"},{"text":"Say, “That's not kind”","to":"stand"}]},"laugh":{"text":"You laugh along. Across the playground, Mariam hears. Her eyes fill with tears and she looks down at her lunch. That night, you can't stop thinking about her face.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"grass","props":[["bench",55,92,1],["child",50,86,0.8,"#ec407a"],["child",65,92,0.9,"#1e88e5"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Say sorry to Mariam the next day","to":"laughsorry"},{"text":"Pretend nothing happened","to":"ignored"}]},"stand":{"text":"“That's not kind,” you say quietly. Everyone goes silent. Then one friend says, “Yeah, you're right.” You pick up your lunch and walk over to Mariam's bench.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"grass","props":[["child",40,92,0.9,"#1e88e5"],["bench",70,92,1],["child",70,86,0.8,"#ec407a"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Sit down next to her","to":"sit"}]},"sit":{"text":"“Can I sit here?” you ask. Mariam looks surprised, then nods shyly. She tells you her family moved here a few weeks ago, and she misses her old friends and her grandmother very much.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"grass","props":[["bench",50,92,1.2],["child",44,86,0.8,"#ec407a"],["child",56,86,0.8,"#1e88e5"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Ask about her home","to":"ask"},{"text":"Share your snack","to":"share"}]},"ask":{"text":"You ask about her home. Her face lights up as she tells you about the mountains, her grandmother's garden, and the big church with golden domes where her family used to go. “We go to church here too,” she says.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"grass","props":[["bench",50,92,1.2],["child",44,86,0.8,"#ec407a"],["child",56,86,0.8,"#1e88e5"],["church",85,84,0.7]]},"choices":[{"text":"Invite her to play","to":"play"}]},"share":{"text":"You break your biscuit in half and give her a piece. She laughs and shares some of her dates with you: sweet and sticky, you've never tasted anything like them!","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"grass","props":[["bench",50,92,1.2],["child",44,86,0.8,"#ec407a"],["child",56,86,0.8,"#1e88e5"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Invite her to play","to":"play"}]},"play":{"text":"When the bell rings for break, you grab Mariam's hand. “Come and play with us!” Soon she is laughing and running with everyone. Nobody is whispering any more.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"grass","props":[["child",30,92,0.9,"#ec407a"],["child",45,92,0.9,"#1e88e5"],["child",60,92,0.9,"#43a047"],["ball",75,92,0.6]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"A new friend","lesson":"Treat others the way you would want to be treated, especially people who feel alone.","verse":"And as ye would that men should do to you, do ye also to them likewise.","ref":"Luke 6:31"}},"laughsorry":{"text":"The next day, you go to Mariam and say, “I'm sorry I laughed. That was wrong.” She is quiet for a moment, then gives you a small smile. “Thank you for saying that.”","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"grass","props":[["bench",55,92,1],["child",50,86,0.8,"#ec407a"],["child",65,92,0.9,"#1e88e5"]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"Saying sorry","lesson":"Unkind laughter hurts. But saying sorry, and meaning it, can begin to heal. Next time, we can choose kindness first.","verse":"And be ye kind one to another, tenderhearted, forgiving one another, even as God for Christ's sake hath forgiven you.","ref":"Ephesians 4:32"}},"ignored":{"text":"You pretend nothing happened. The next day the whole class knows you laughed at Mariam, and some children start copying her accent too, because you did.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"grass","props":[["child",35,92,0.9,"#ec407a"],["child",48,92,0.9,"#43a047"],["child",60,92,0.9,"#fb8c00"],["child",85,92,0.9,"#1e88e5"]]},"sfx":"sting","choices":[{"text":"Stand up for her now","to":"ignored_fix"},{"text":"Keep quiet","to":"ignored_worse"}]},"ignored_fix":{"text":"“Stop it,” you say. “I was wrong to laugh, and so are you.” The class goes quiet. Mariam looks at you in surprise. It takes time, but slowly she begins to trust you.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"grass","props":[["child",35,92,0.9,"#ec407a"],["child",48,92,0.9,"#43a047"],["child",60,92,0.9,"#fb8c00"],["child",85,92,0.9,"#1e88e5"]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"Standing up at last","lesson":"Your laughter spread unkindness, and standing up stopped it. Owning our wrong helps others do the same.","verse":"And be ye kind one to another, tenderhearted, forgiving one another.","ref":"Ephesians 4:32"}},"ignored_worse":{"text":"You keep quiet, and the teasing grows. One morning Mariam's seat is empty: her parents have moved her to another school because she was so unhappy. The teacher talks to the class about kindness, and everyone knows where it started. Even your own friends begin to keep their distance.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"grass","props":[["child",35,92,0.9,"#ec407a"]]},"sfx":"sting","end":{"type":"missed","title":"An empty seat","lesson":"Unkindness that is never put right can drive someone away, and it spreads. Being friendly, and saying sorry quickly, stops harm before it grows.","verse":"A man that hath friends must shew himself friendly.","ref":"Proverbs 18:24"}}}},{"id":"broken-lamp","category":"life","icon":"🪔","title":"The Broken Lamp","summary":"You weren't supposed to play ball indoors, and now the icon lamp is broken.","passage":{"label":"1 John 1","book":"1 John","chapter":1,"verse":9},"scenes":{"start":{"text":"You are playing ball in the living room, even though you know you shouldn't. The ball bounces off the wall and knocks over the little oil lamp in front of the family icons. Crash! It breaks into pieces on the floor.","art":{"sky":"indoor","ground":"room","props":[["icon",40,58,1],["broken",40,92,1],["ball",62,92,0.6],["child",75,90,1,"#1e88e5"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Hide the pieces","to":"hide"},{"text":"Tell your mother right away","to":"tell"},{"text":"Blame the cat","to":"blame"}]},"hide":{"text":"You quickly sweep the pieces under the sofa. A little later your mother comes in. “Where is the icon lamp?” she asks. Your heart is pounding.","art":{"sky":"indoor","ground":"room","props":[["icon",40,58,1],["person",60,90,1.1,"#c2185b"],["child",75,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Tell the truth now","to":"tell"},{"text":"Say you don't know","to":"lie"}]},"lie":{"text":"“I don't know,” you mumble. That night you can't sleep. The icon corner looks dark without its little light.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"room","props":[["icon",40,58,1],["person",58,90,1.1,"#c2185b"],["child",70,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Get up and tell the truth","to":"liesorry"},{"text":"Keep the secret","to":"found"}]},"blame":{"text":"“The cat did it!” you say. Your mother shuts the cat outside in the rain as a punishment. The poor cat meows at the door. You feel awful.","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"street","props":[["house",50,86,1.2],["cat",50,93,0.8]]},"choices":[{"text":"Tell the truth","to":"tell"},{"text":"Keep quiet and let the cat take the blame","to":"catrain"}]},"tell":{"text":"You tell your mother what happened. She is sad about the lamp, but she kneels down and hugs you. “Thank you for telling me the truth. That matters more than any lamp.” Together you sweep up the pieces, and you offer to buy a new lamp with your pocket money.","art":{"sky":"indoor","ground":"room","props":[["icon",40,58,1],["person",55,90,1.1,"#c2185b"],["child",67,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Light the new lamp together","to":"light"}]},"light":{"text":"A week later, you and your mother light the new icon lamp together. Its little flame glows warmly in front of the icons. You say a prayer of thanks. Your heart feels as light as the flame.","art":{"sky":"indoor","ground":"room","props":[["icon",45,56,1],["lamp",45,74,1],["child",62,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"],["person",75,90,1,"#c2185b"]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"Forgiven","lesson":"When we say sorry and tell the truth, God and the people who love us are ready to forgive.","verse":"If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins.","ref":"1 John 1:9"}},"liesorry":{"text":"At last you get up, go to your mother and tell her everything. She hugs you tightly. “Thank you for telling me the truth. I forgive you.”","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"room","props":[["icon",40,58,1],["person",58,90,1.1,"#c2185b"],["child",70,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"The truth sets the heart free","lesson":"Hiding what we did wrong makes our heart heavy. Confessing it brings forgiveness and peace.","verse":"He that covereth his sins shall not prosper: but whoso confesseth and forsaketh them shall have mercy.","ref":"Proverbs 28:13"}},"found":{"text":"A few days later, your mother moves the sofa to clean and finds the broken pieces. She looks at you for a long time. “Did you do this?”","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"room","props":[["broken",40,92,1],["person",55,90,1.1,"#c2185b"],["child",72,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"]]},"sfx":"tension","choices":[{"text":"Tell the truth at last","to":"found_fix"},{"text":"Blame your little brother","to":"found_worse"}]},"catrain":{"text":"You say nothing. The poor cat meows at the door in the rain. Then it goes quiet. When you peek outside, the cat is gone.","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"street","props":[["house",50,86,1.2],["cat",50,93,0.8]]},"sfx":"thunder","choices":[{"text":"Wake your mother and tell her everything","to":"catrain_fix"},{"text":"Go back to bed","to":"catrain_worse"}]},"found_fix":{"text":"“Yes,” you whisper. “I'm sorry I hid it.” She is sad, but she hugs you. “Thank you for telling me now. Next time, tell me straight away.” It takes a while before she trusts your word again.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"room","props":[["broken",40,92,1],["person",55,90,1.1,"#c2185b"],["child",72,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"Truth at last","lesson":"Hiding it made things worse, but the truth, even late, begins to heal.","verse":"Lying lips are abomination to the LORD: but they that deal truly are his delight.","ref":"Proverbs 12:22"}},"found_worse":{"text":"“It was my brother!” Your little brother is punished and cries himself to sleep, saying it wasn't him. The next day your grandmother mentions she saw you playing ball in that room. Now there are two lies, a punished brother, and a mother who doesn't know when to believe you. You lose your pocket money for a month, and something far more precious: her trust.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"room","props":[["broken",40,92,1],["moon",82,16,1],["child",72,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"]]},"sfx":"sting","end":{"type":"missed","title":"One lie becomes three","lesson":"Each lie needed another, and an innocent person got hurt. Lies grow; the truth sets us free.","verse":"And ye shall know the truth, and the truth shall make you free.","ref":"John 8:32"}},"catrain_fix":{"text":"You tell your mother everything. Together you search with a torch and find the cat shivering under the neighbour's car. You dry it by the fire. Your mother is sad about the lie, but glad you told her.","art":{"sky":"dawn","ground":"street","props":[["house",50,86,1.2],["cat",50,93,0.8]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"Brought in from the rain","lesson":"Blaming someone else hurt an innocent animal; telling the truth brought it home.","verse":"Thou shalt not bear false witness against thy neighbour.","ref":"Exodus 20:16"}},"catrain_worse":{"text":"You pull the blanket over your head. In the morning the cat is nowhere to be found. For three days your whole family searches the streets and puts up posters. When a neighbour finally brings it home, thin and frightened, your mother finds a piece of the lamp stuck in your sock, and she knows. You blamed an innocent animal and let your family worry for days.","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"street","props":[["house",50,86,1.2],["cat",50,93,0.8]]},"sfx":"thunder","end":{"type":"missed","title":"The cat in the rain","lesson":"Letting someone else take the blame caused real suffering. Blaming others is a lie that hurts the innocent.","verse":"Thou shalt not bear false witness against thy neighbour.","ref":"Exodus 20:16"}}}},{"id":"last-slice","category":"life","icon":"🥧","title":"The Last Slice","summary":"Grandmother's pie is almost gone, and there's only one slice left.","passage":{"label":"2 Corinthians 9","book":"2 Corinthians","chapter":9,"verse":7},"scenes":{"start":{"text":"Grandmother has baked her famous apple pie. Everyone has had a slice. Now there is just one slice left on the plate. Your little brother didn't get any, and your friend Luka, who is visiting, is looking at it too.","art":{"sky":"indoor","ground":"room","props":[["table",50,90,1.2],["pie",50,76,1],["child",25,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"],["child",75,90,0.7,"#43a047"],["child",88,90,0.9,"#fb8c00"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Eat it quickly","to":"eat"},{"text":"Share it","to":"share"},{"text":"Give it away","to":"give"}]},"eat":{"text":"You grab the slice and gobble it up. It's delicious! But then you see your little brother's sad face, and Luka looking at his feet. The pie doesn't feel so nice in your tummy now.","art":{"sky":"indoor","ground":"room","props":[["table",50,90,1.2],["child",40,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"],["child",65,90,0.7,"#43a047"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Make it right","to":"fix"},{"text":"Shrug and go and play","to":"selfish"}]},"fix":{"text":"“I'm sorry,” you say. “That wasn't fair.” You fetch your box of biscuits and share them with your brother and Luka. Soon everyone is smiling again, and Grandmother winks at you.","art":{"sky":"indoor","ground":"room","props":[["table",50,90,1.2],["child",40,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"],["child",55,90,0.7,"#43a047"],["child",70,90,0.9,"#fb8c00"]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"Making it right","lesson":"It's easy to think of ourselves first. But it's never too late to share, and sharing makes everyone happier.","verse":"It is more blessed to give than to receive.","ref":"Acts 20:35"}},"share":{"text":"You cut the slice into three small pieces: one for your brother, one for Luka and one for you. It's only a little bite each, but everyone smiles. Somehow it tastes even better shared.","art":{"sky":"indoor","ground":"room","props":[["table",50,90,1.2],["pie",50,76,0.7],["child",35,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"],["child",52,90,0.7,"#43a047"],["child",68,90,0.9,"#fb8c00"]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"Better together","lesson":"Sharing turns a little into enough for everyone, and God loves a cheerful giver.","verse":"for God loveth a cheerful giver.","ref":"2 Corinthians 9:7"}},"give":{"text":"You give the slice to your little brother and Luka to share. Grandmother sees it. Later she calls you into the kitchen, and there, hidden away, is a small slice she saved just for you! “A kind heart,” she says, “never goes without.”","art":{"sky":"indoor","ground":"room","props":[["table",50,90,1.2],["pie",50,76,0.8],["person",65,90,1.1,"#8e24aa"],["child",40,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"A generous heart","lesson":"Giving to others fills our hearts with joy, just as Jesus taught.","verse":"It is more blessed to give than to receive.","ref":"Acts 20:35"}},"selfish":{"text":"You shrug and run off to play. Your little brother starts to cry, and Luka quietly asks to go home. Grandmother watches from the kitchen door.","art":{"sky":"indoor","ground":"room","props":[["table",50,90,1.2],["child",30,90,0.7,"#43a047"],["child",75,90,0.9,"#fb8c00"]]},"sfx":"tension","choices":[{"text":"Go back and say sorry","to":"selfish_fix"},{"text":"Keep playing","to":"selfish_worse"}]},"selfish_fix":{"text":"You go back and say sorry to your brother and Luka, and share your own sweets. Luka decides to stay after all. Grandmother winks at you.","art":{"sky":"indoor","ground":"room","props":[["table",50,90,1.2],["child",30,90,0.7,"#43a047"],["child",75,90,0.9,"#fb8c00"]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"Turning back","lesson":"Selfishness spoiled the afternoon; turning back quickly saved it.","verse":"Look not every man on his own things, but every man also on the things of others.","ref":"Philippians 2:4"}},"selfish_worse":{"text":"You keep playing. Luka goes home and tells his parents he doesn't want to come again. Your brother won't speak to you all evening. At dinner, Grandmother says quietly, “I baked that pie for all of you to share.” She looks so hurt. The next Sunday, there's no pie for anyone.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"room","props":[["table",50,90,1.2],["child",30,90,0.7,"#43a047"]]},"sfx":"sting","end":{"type":"missed","title":"A spoiled afternoon","lesson":"Thinking only of ourselves hurts the people we love and spoils good gifts for everyone.","verse":"The liberal soul shall be made fat: and he that watereth shall be watered also himself.","ref":"Proverbs 11:25"}}}},{"id":"sunday-morning","category":"life","icon":"⛪","title":"Sunday Morning","summary":"It's Sunday, your bed is warm, and church starts soon.","passage":{"label":"Psalm 122","book":"Psalms","chapter":122,"verse":1},"scenes":{"start":{"text":"It's Sunday morning. Your bed is warm and cosy. Downstairs your family is getting ready for the Divine Liturgy. “Time to get up!” your father calls. You pull the blanket over your head.","art":{"sky":"dawn","ground":"room","props":[["bed",50,90,1.2],["window",75,50,1]]},"choices":[{"text":"Stay in bed a bit longer","to":"stay"},{"text":"Get up and get ready","to":"up"},{"text":"Pull the blanket up and go back to sleep","to":"overslept"}]},"stay":{"text":"You close your eyes again. Then you remember: today is the day your cousin is being baptised at church! You would miss it! You jump out of bed.","art":{"sky":"dawn","ground":"room","props":[["bed",50,90,1.2],["child",68,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Hurry to get ready","to":"up"}]},"up":{"text":"You wash your face, put on your Sunday clothes and join your family. At the church door, the smell of incense and the golden glow of candles welcome you in.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"grass","props":[["church",55,86,1.3],["child",25,92,0.8,"#1e88e5"],["person",35,92,1,"#5d4037"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Light a candle","to":"candle"},{"text":"Go and stand with your friends","to":"friends"}]},"candle":{"text":"Your mother gives you a thin beeswax candle. You light it and place it before the icon of the Theotokos, and you pray for your grandfather who is ill. The little flame flickers bravely among all the others.","art":{"sky":"indoor","ground":"room","props":[["icon",45,52,1],["candles",45,86,1.2],["child",68,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Join in the singing","to":"sing"}]},"friends":{"text":"You stand near your friends. You're tempted to whisper and giggle, but then the choir begins to sing. The words are beautiful: “Holy God, Holy Mighty, Holy Immortal, have mercy on us.”","art":{"sky":"indoor","ground":"room","props":[["icon",50,52,1],["candles",30,86,0.8],["child",60,90,0.8,"#1e88e5"],["child",72,90,0.8,"#43a047"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Join in the singing","to":"sing"}]},"sing":{"text":"You sing along with everyone. Then comes the joyful moment of Holy Communion, and afterwards the priest gives you a piece of blessed bread. Your cousin is baptised, and everyone cheers. On the way home you realise it was the best part of your whole week.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"grass","props":[["church",50,86,1.2],["child",30,92,0.8,"#1e88e5"],["child",42,92,0.7,"#ec407a"],["person",70,92,1,"#5d4037"],["light",50,30,0.6]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"The best part of the week","lesson":"Sunday is the Lord's day. Going to church together fills our hearts with joy and brings us close to God and to each other.","verse":"I was glad when they said unto me, Let us go into the house of the LORD.","ref":"Psalm 122:1"}},"overslept":{"text":"You snuggle down and fall fast asleep. When you wake, the house is silent. Everyone has gone to church without you, and today is your cousin's baptism.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"room","props":[["bed",50,90,1.2],["child",68,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"],["window",75,50,1]]},"sfx":"tension","choices":[{"text":"Get dressed and run to church","to":"overslept_fix"},{"text":"Stay home and play","to":"overslept_worse"}]},"overslept_fix":{"text":"You dress as fast as you can and run all the way. You slip in just as the priest is baptising your cousin. You missed the start of the Liturgy, but you're there for the joy.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"room","props":[["bed",50,90,1.2],["child",68,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"],["window",75,50,1]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"Just in time","lesson":"Sleeping in nearly made you miss a holy day, but hurrying to God's house brought you into the joy.","verse":"I was glad when they said unto me, Let us go into the house of the LORD.","ref":"Psalm 122:1"}},"overslept_worse":{"text":"You stay home and play alone all morning. When your family comes back, they're full of joy. Your cousin kept looking for you during the whole service, and there's a family photo with everyone in it except you. Your grandmother says quietly that she saved you a seat. A once-in-a-lifetime day, and you slept and played through it.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"room","props":[["bed",50,90,1.2],["window",75,50,1],["child",68,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"]]},"sfx":"bell","end":{"type":"missed","title":"Asleep on the Lord's day","lesson":"Choosing sleep and play over the Lord's day meant missing a once-in-a-lifetime blessing with your family.","verse":"Not forsaking the assembling of ourselves together.","ref":"Hebrews 10:25"}}}},{"id":"baby-in-basket","category":"bible","icon":"🧺","title":"The Baby in the Basket","summary":"Your best friend Miriam has a secret: a baby brother hidden from Pharaoh.","passage":{"label":"Exodus 2","book":"Exodus","chapter":2,"verse":1},"scenes":{"start":{"text":"You live in Egypt, where God's people are slaves. Pharaoh has made a cruel law against baby boys. Your best friend Miriam whispers a secret: “My mother has hidden my baby brother for three months. She can't hide him any longer. Tomorrow she will put him in a basket on the river.”","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["house",30,86,1.1],["child",55,92,0.9,"#ec407a"],["child",68,92,0.9,"#26a69a"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Promise to help Miriam","to":"help"},{"text":"Say it's too dangerous","to":"danger"}]},"danger":{"text":"“It's too dangerous!” you whisper. Miriam's eyes fill with tears. “But he's my brother. I have to help him. Please come with me.”","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"street","props":[["child",45,92,0.9,"#ec407a"],["child",60,92,0.9,"#26a69a"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Go with her after all","to":"help"},{"text":"Go and play by the market instead","to":"play"}]},"play":{"text":"You go and play by the market. The crowds are huge and you wander far from home. Suddenly you realise you don't know where you are, and the sun is setting.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"street","props":[["town",50,84,1],["crowd",30,90,0.8],["child",75,92,0.9,"#26a69a"]]},"sfx":"crowd","choices":[{"text":"Ask a kind-looking woman for help","to":"play_fix"},{"text":"Keep wandering on your own","to":"play_worse"}]},"help":{"text":"Early the next morning, Miriam's mother lays the baby in a basket made of bulrushes, sealed so no water can get in. She puts it among the reeds at the edge of the river, and kisses the baby goodbye. You and Miriam hide in the tall grass to watch.","art":{"sky":"dawn","ground":"shore","props":[["basket",50,86,0.9],["tree",20,88,0.8],["child",75,92,0.8,"#ec407a"],["child",85,92,0.8,"#26a69a"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Keep watching quietly","to":"watch"},{"text":"Go and fetch some food","to":"food"}]},"food":{"text":"You're hungry, so you run home to fetch bread. When you come back out of breath, Miriam grabs your arm. “Look! Someone's coming!”","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"shore","props":[["basket",50,86,0.9],["child",80,92,0.8,"#ec407a"],["bread",88,92,0.6]]},"choices":[{"text":"Hide and watch","to":"watch"}]},"watch":{"text":"Pharaoh's daughter comes down to the river to wash, with her maids. She sees the basket among the reeds and sends a maid to fetch it. When she opens it, the baby is crying. “This is one of the Hebrews' children,” she says, and her face fills with pity.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"shore","props":[["person",40,92,1.1,"#f9a825"],["person",52,92,1,"#26a69a"],["basket",46,88,0.7],["child",82,92,0.8,"#ec407a"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Tell Miriam to stay hidden","to":"hidden"},{"text":"Whisper, “Go on, Miriam! Speak to her!”","to":"brave"}]},"hidden":{"text":"“Stay hidden!” you whisper. But Miriam takes a deep breath. “I have to try,” she says, and she steps out of the reeds.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"shore","props":[["child",60,92,0.9,"#ec407a"],["person",35,92,1.1,"#f9a825"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Watch","to":"nurse"}]},"brave":{"text":"Miriam squeezes your hand, takes a deep breath and walks bravely up to the princess.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"shore","props":[["child",60,92,0.9,"#ec407a"],["person",35,92,1.1,"#f9a825"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Watch","to":"nurse"}]},"nurse":{"text":"“Shall I go and find a Hebrew woman to nurse the baby for you?” Miriam asks. “Go,” says Pharaoh's daughter. Miriam runs, and brings back the baby's own mother! The princess pays her to care for him. When he grows up, she names him Moses, “because I drew him out of the water.”","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"shore","props":[["person",35,92,1.1,"#f9a825"],["person",55,92,1,"#8d6e63"],["child",68,92,0.8,"#ec407a"],["child",80,92,0.8,"#26a69a"],["light",50,40,0.6]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"Drawn out of the water","lesson":"God watched over baby Moses, and used a brave girl, and a loyal friend, to save him. God had great plans for him.","verse":"And she called his name Moses: and she said, Because I drew him out of the water.","ref":"Exodus 2:10"}},"play_fix":{"text":"A kind woman walks you home. Miriam is there, bursting with news: Pharaoh's daughter found her brother, and their mother gets to nurse him! You're glad, but sorry you weren't beside her.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"street","props":[["town",50,84,1],["crowd",30,90,0.8],["child",75,92,0.9,"#26a69a"]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"Found again","lesson":"You left your friend when she needed you and got lost yourself. Asking for help brought you home; next time, stay with those who need you.","verse":"A friend loveth at all times.","ref":"Proverbs 17:17"}},"play_worse":{"text":"You wander on until it's dark and you're far from home, frightened and alone. At last a guard brings you back to your street late at night, where your parents have been searching for hours. Miriam won't come out to see you. She faced the princess by herself, and her brother was saved, but she needed a friend, and you weren't there.","art":{"sky":"night","ground":"street","props":[["town",50,84,1],["moon",82,16,1],["child",75,92,0.9,"#26a69a"]]},"sfx":"wind","end":{"type":"missed","title":"Not there for a friend","lesson":"Choosing to play when a friend needed you left you lost and her alone. True friends stand together in hard times.","verse":"Two are better than one. For if they fall, the one will lift up his fellow.","ref":"Ecclesiastes 4:9-10"}}}},{"id":"wave-and-icon","category":"saints","icon":"🌊","title":"The Wave and the Icon","summary":"You live with Saint Herman on a small island in Alaska. One day the sea rises.","passage":{"label":"Psalm 91","book":"Psalms","chapter":91,"verse":1},"scenes":{"start":{"text":"Far away in Alaska, on Spruce Island, lives a humble monk called Father Herman. He came from Russia to share the Gospel, and he looks after orphan children like you. He teaches you to read, to pray, and to love God and one another. Today he is working in his little garden.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"shore","props":[["person",40,92,1.1,"#5d4037","halo"],["child",55,92,0.8,"#26a69a"],["child",65,92,0.7,"#ec407a"],["tree",85,88,1]]},"choices":[{"text":"Help him in the garden","to":"garden"},{"text":"Run off to play on the beach","to":"beach"}]},"garden":{"text":"You help Father Herman pull weeds. He tells you, “From this day, from this hour, from this minute, let us love God above all.” You like working beside him. He is always kind and never in a hurry.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"grass","props":[["person",40,92,1.1,"#5d4037","halo"],["child",56,92,0.8,"#26a69a"],["tree",80,88,1]]},"choices":[{"text":"Go down to the shore with the others","to":"shore"}]},"beach":{"text":"You run down to the beach with the younger children, skipping stones across the water. The sea is calm and sparkling.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"shore","props":[["child",35,92,0.8,"#26a69a"],["child",48,92,0.7,"#ec407a"],["child",60,92,0.6,"#fb8c00"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Keep playing","to":"shore"}]},"shore":{"text":"Suddenly people shout from the village. The ground has shaken, and far out at sea a huge wave is rising, coming towards the island! Everyone is running. The little ones are crying and don't know where to go.","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"shore","props":[["child",40,92,0.7,"#ec407a"],["child",52,92,0.6,"#fb8c00"],["person",75,92,1,"#6d4c41"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Run up the hill as fast as you can","to":"run"},{"text":"Grab the little ones' hands and run together","to":"little"}]},"run":{"text":"You race up the hill alone, as fast as your legs will go. At the top you turn around, and see that the little ones are still down on the beach, crying.","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"hills","props":[["child",60,86,0.8,"#26a69a"],["child",25,94,0.5,"#ec407a"],["child",33,94,0.5,"#fb8c00"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Run back down for them","to":"back"},{"text":"Stay safe at the top","to":"alone"}]},"alone":{"text":"You stay at the top, your heart pounding. Down on the beach the little ones are crying, and the great wave is coming closer and closer.","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"hills","props":[["child",60,86,0.8,"#26a69a"],["light",25,70,0.7]]},"sfx":"waves","choices":[{"text":"Run back down for them after all","to":"back"},{"text":"Hide behind the rocks and cover your eyes","to":"alone_worse"}]},"back":{"text":"You run back down, grab the little ones by the hand, and bring them to Father Herman.","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"shore","props":[["child",45,92,0.8,"#26a69a"],["child",55,92,0.6,"#ec407a"],["person",70,92,1.1,"#5d4037","halo"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Stay close to Father Herman","to":"icon"}]},"little":{"text":"You grab a small hand in each of yours. “Come on, stay with me!” You run together towards Father Herman, who is walking calmly towards the sea.","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"shore","props":[["child",45,92,0.8,"#26a69a"],["child",55,92,0.6,"#ec407a"],["person",70,92,1.1,"#5d4037","halo"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Stay close to Father Herman","to":"icon"}]},"icon":{"text":"Father Herman carries an icon of the Mother of God down to the shore and sets it on the sand. The Church remembers that he prayed and told the people, “Do not be afraid. The water will not go past the place where the holy icon stands.” The great wave rushes in, and stops right there, and goes back to the sea.","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"shore","props":[["icon",50,86,1.4],["person",35,92,1.1,"#5d4037","halo"],["child",68,92,0.7,"#26a69a"],["child",76,92,0.6,"#ec407a"],["light",50,55,0.9]]},"choices":[{"text":"Thank God together","to":"thanks"}]},"thanks":{"text":"Everyone falls to their knees and thanks God. Father Herman smiles at you. “You did not leave the little ones. That was love, and love is the most important thing.” The icon stays on the shore for a long time, and the people remember that day for generations.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"shore","props":[["icon",50,86,1.2],["person",35,92,1.1,"#5d4037","halo"],["child",62,92,0.8,"#26a69a"],["child",72,92,0.6,"#ec407a"],["crowd",86,90,0.6]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"Safe in God's care","lesson":"Saint Herman trusted God completely, and taught the children to love one another. We can trust God in danger, and care for others while we do.","verse":"I will say of the LORD, He is my refuge and my fortress: my God; in him will I trust.","ref":"Psalm 91:2"}},"alone_worse":{"text":"You hide behind the rocks. When you dare to look again, the wave has stopped at the holy icon, and Father Herman is carrying the little ones up the hill. Trying to climb down, you slip on the wet rocks and cut your knee. Later a little girl says, “You ran away and left us.” Father Herman bandages your knee and says gently, “Next time, love will make you brave.” You have never felt so ashamed.","art":{"sky":"storm","ground":"hills","props":[["child",60,86,0.8,"#26a69a"]]},"sfx":"sting","end":{"type":"missed","title":"Running away alone","lesson":"Fear made you think only of yourself. Loving others means helping those weaker than us, even when we are afraid.","verse":"Bear ye one another's burdens, and so fulfil the law of Christ.","ref":"Galatians 6:2"}}}},{"id":"spelling-test","category":"life","icon":"📝","title":"The Spelling Test","summary":"You didn't study for today's test, and the answers are right there.","passage":{"label":"Colossians 3","book":"Colossians","chapter":3,"verse":23},"scenes":{"start":{"text":"It's the big spelling test, and you forgot to study. Your mind goes blank at the third word. Then you notice: the girl next to you has her paper turned so you can see all her answers.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"room","props":[["table",50,90,1.2],["child",40,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"],["child",62,90,0.9,"#ec407a"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Copy her answers","to":"copy"},{"text":"Do your best on your own","to":"own"},{"text":"Look away and ask to move seats","to":"move"}]},"copy":{"text":"You copy the answers quickly. A week later, the teacher hands back the tests: you got full marks, and your name is read out as top of the class! But the teacher looks at you and at your neighbour's paper, and asks you to stay behind after class.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"room","props":[["table",50,90,1.2],["child",40,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"],["person",70,90,1.1,"#5d4037"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Tell the teacher the truth","to":"confess"},{"text":"Say you studied really hard","to":"liedup"}]},"confess":{"text":"Your cheeks burn, but you tell her the truth. The teacher is quiet, then says, “Thank you for being honest. That takes courage.” You have to take the test again, and your mark isn't as high this time, but you studied properly, and it's really yours.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"room","props":[["child",40,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"],["person",60,90,1.1,"#5d4037"]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"Honest at last","lesson":"Copying took something that wasn't ours. Owning up is hard, but it put things right, and an honest mark is worth more than a borrowed one.","verse":"A false balance is abomination to the LORD: but a just weight is his delight.","ref":"Proverbs 11:1"}},"liedup":{"text":"“I studied really hard,” you say. The teacher doesn't believe you. She writes a note home and asks your parents to come in and see her.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"room","props":[["table",60,90,0.8],["child",60,86,0.8,"#1e88e5"]]},"sfx":"tension","choices":[{"text":"Tell your parents the truth before the meeting","to":"liedup_fix"},{"text":"Stick to your story","to":"liedup_worse"}]},"own":{"text":"You take a deep breath and do your best. Some words you know, some you guess. A week later you get your mark back: six out of ten. Not great, but it's all yours. The teacher writes: “Honest work. Let's practise together.”","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"room","props":[["table",50,90,1.2],["child",40,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"],["person",68,90,1,"#5d4037"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Practise with your teacher","to":"practise"}]},"move":{"text":"You put up your hand. “Please may I sit somewhere else? I can see someone's answers.” The teacher looks surprised, then smiles and moves you. You do your best on your own.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"room","props":[["table",50,90,1.2],["child",30,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"],["person",65,90,1,"#5d4037"]]},"choices":[{"text":"Wait for your results","to":"own"}]},"practise":{"text":"Every day that week you practise with your teacher and your mother. On the next test you get nine out of ten, all by yourself! You feel proud, not because of the number, but because you worked for it honestly.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"room","props":[["table",50,90,1.2],["child",45,90,0.9,"#1e88e5"],["light",50,40,0.5]]},"end":{"type":"happy","title":"Honest and growing","lesson":"Doing our work honestly, as for God, makes us stronger, and there's real joy in what we truly earn.","verse":"And whatsoever ye do, do it heartily, as to the Lord, and not unto men.","ref":"Colossians 3:23"}},"liedup_fix":{"text":"That evening you tell your parents everything. They're disappointed, but proud that you told them yourself. At the meeting you say sorry to your teacher and take the test again, honestly.","art":{"sky":"day","ground":"room","props":[["table",60,90,0.8],["child",60,86,0.8,"#1e88e5"]]},"end":{"type":"learn","title":"Owning up","lesson":"Cheating and lying took something that wasn't yours, but confessing began to put it right.","verse":"He that covereth his sins shall not prosper: but whoso confesseth and forsaketh them shall have mercy.","ref":"Proverbs 28:13"}},"liedup_worse":{"text":"At the meeting you stick to your story, but the teacher lays your answers next to your neighbour's: the same mistakes in the same places. Your parents look at you in silence. Your test is marked zero, you're taken off the class trip, and your neighbour is angry because she was questioned too. Now nobody believes you, even when you're telling the truth.","art":{"sky":"dusk","ground":"room","props":[["table",60,90,0.8],["child",60,86,0.8,"#1e88e5"]]},"sfx":"sting","end":{"type":"missed","title":"One wrong on top of another","lesson":"Cheating and lying took away trust, a fair mark and a friend. It's never too late to confess and start again.","verse":"The lip of truth shall be established for ever: but a lying tongue is but for a moment.","ref":"Proverbs 12:19"}}}}],"bible":"https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/"}</script></div></section><section aria-labelledby="colouring-heading" class="bg-paper scroll-mt-24" id="colouring"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-9 sm:px-8 sm:py-12"><div class="border-purple-deep/15 flex flex-col gap-4 border-b pb-5 sm:flex-row sm:items-end sm:justify-between sm:gap-8 kk-banner kk-banner--light" style="--kb1:#C8325A;--kb2:#EE6A8C"><span class="kk-banner__badge" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-core/assets/kids-extras/cards/crayons.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><div><p class="text-purple text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.22em] uppercase">Create and colour</p><h2 class="font-display text-purple-deep mt-2 text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl" id="colouring-heading">Colouring Bible Scenes</h2></div><div class="flex items-end justify-between gap-5 sm:max-w-xl sm:flex-1"><p class="text-ink max-w-xl text-sm leading-6 sm:text-right">Printable Bible scenes featuring Resurrection, Bible characters, and Easter imagery.</p><div aria-label="Scroll coloring pages" class="hidden shrink-0 gap-2 sm:flex"><button aria-label="Scroll coloring pages left" class="border-yellow bg-yellow text-purple-deep grid size-10 place-items-center rou