<p>Kids Corner is made for children and grown-ups to enjoy side by side. A few minutes together is better than a long session alone.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Start with the Bible Adventure Trail.</strong> One stop per sitting is plenty. Let your child tap through the steps, and read the story aloud together.</li>
<li><strong>Pray the Grow prayer together</strong> at the end of each stop, and try the Prayer Garden at bedtime.</li>
<li><strong>Use the Bible reader</strong> for the "real thing": the trail's story is a simple retelling, and the Read button opens the full passage.</li>
<li><strong>Print the certificate</strong> when a trail is finished and celebrate it together.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Your child is safe here</h3>
<p>Kids Corner was built so that children can read, play and pray without giving anything away about themselves.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>No accounts and no personal information.</strong> Kids Corner never asks for an email address, an age, a photo, a phone number or a location. A nickname for the greeting is optional and stays on this device.</li>
<li><strong>Progress stays on your device.</strong> Stars, badges, reading, bookmarks and garden flowers are kept in this browser. Nothing about your child is sent to the website unless you choose to use a Pilgrim Key.</li>
<li><strong>A Pilgrim Key keeps only progress.</strong> If your child saves with a Pilgrim Key, the website keeps only the progress (stars, badges, reading and game scores). It is filed under a scrambled form of the key, so no one, not even the website owner, can tell whose progress it is or link it to a person.</li>
<li><strong>A nickname never leaves the device.</strong> A first name or nickname for the greeting stays on this device and in the browser's own saved passwords. Names are checked for bad language.</li>
<li><strong>No chat, no messages, no adverts.</strong> Children cannot talk to strangers here, and nobody can contact them through Kids Corner.</li>
<li><strong>You stay in control.</strong> "Forget my key" deletes the saved progress from the website at any time. Clearing the browser's data removes everything from the device.</li>
</ul>
<p>Some sections play cartoons hosted by video websites, which have their own policies. We recommend watching those together.</p><div class="kk-voice-settings" data-kjt-voice-settings></div></div></div></section></div></main><style id="kjt-media-pic-css">button.aspect-video>img[data-kjt-added-picture]~div.place-items-center{display:none!important}</style></main><footer class="bfp-footer bfp"><div class="bfp-container"><p><strong>Knowing Jesus Today</strong></p><p class="kjt-footer-sitemap"><a href="https://knowingjesus.today/site-map/">🗺️ Site Map</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://knowingjesus.today/about/">About us</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://knowingjesus.today/imprint/">Imprint</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://knowingjesus.today/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a></p><p class="kjt-footer-note">Christ is in our midst ☦ He is and ever shall be.</p></div><div class="bfp-container kjt-footer-legal"><p>&copy; 2026 Knowing Jesus Today &middot; Pictures, logo and text: all rights reserved &middot; Website code: free software (<a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.html" rel="license noopener" target="_blank">GNU GPL v2 or later</a>)</p></div></footer><script type="speculationrules">
